1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:03,010
Visit our website for more: turkision.com

2
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,590
No living being was harmed during
the filming of this series.

3
00:02:08,945 --> 00:02:12,025
Bursa Palace

4
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,279
We'll fight.

5
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,879
We can't lose to
the Turks anymore.

6
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,999
We have to do something.

7
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,559
How could you lose Kopruhisar?

8
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:42,959
Do the Byzantine soldiers carry
their swords only to show off?

9
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:47,439
If people are led by others who don't
know how to fight instead of commanders...

10
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:50,199
...the inevitable ending is near.

11
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:54,319
But first of all, the commander
needs to know his place.

12
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:59,159
Are Lords talking now,
who couldn’t protect their people?

13
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:13,959
You have commanders who
have seen dozens of battles.

14
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:20,519
Lords don't need to be afraid of us.

15
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:24,839
Those who should be afraid are the Turks.

16
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:30,559
You were there when our armies
set their tribes on fire, Commander Mateus.

17
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:34,239
We stopped the help Lord
Valens sent from Konya, too.

18
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:37,719
How could Osman do that?

19
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:40,999
You underestimated Osman...

20
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:43,199
...and the price for it was Kopruhisar.

21
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:46,879
Osman has the Lord of Kopruhisar.

22
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,559
No, Lord.

23
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,879
Osman does not have
Petrus, Lord of Kopruhisar...

24
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,319
but I do.

25
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:18,279
Leo.

26
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:37,639
Look what those Turks did to us.

27
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:58,319
Anyone that sleeps before we
take the revenge for this...

28
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:01,159
...will lose their eyes...

29
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,919
...my friends.

30
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:12,839
Those who dream of taking revenge on us
will beg for forgiveness when they wake up.

31
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:17,159
Or when they wake up to our
swords on their necks.

32
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:21,639
The sleep of a fool is deep, brother.

33
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:24,759
No one expected that we
would conquer Kopruhisar.

34
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:32,719
Kopruhisar's conquests will be a
symbol of our victory always.

35
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,559
Osman Bey, what's your next goal?

36
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:42,319
It looks like your soldiers
are turning this into a race.

37
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,559
Is that so?

38
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:49,359
My sons.

39
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:52,919
So, you are curious about my plans.

40
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:56,119
Tell me.

41
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:58,399
Where will we go next?

42
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:01,999
We both have different ideas, father.

43
00:06:02,619 --> 00:06:09,390
Tell us our destination, so we
can determine the winner.

44
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,479
My brothers, protect the Princes.

45
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,119
Stop.

46
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,919
Wait.

47
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:41,319
If this arrow...

48
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:46,839
...belonged to our enemies...

49
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,239
...then...

50
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:54,679
...it would strike us instead
of the ground.

51
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:16,919
My sons, until I return, think
about where I will go next.

52
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,479
Let's see who will be the winner.

53
00:07:48,080 --> 00:07:49,239
Boran Alp.

54
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,839
Where are they taking my father?

55
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:55,439
I know many secrets of my Bey, Orhan Bey.

56
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:57,639
But this is not one of them.

57
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:02,639
Father said that they are
allies, but who are they?

58
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:11,999
Osman crossed the Iine.

59
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:17,559
Kopruhisar, conquered by Osman, is
sacred for us, Lord Valens.

60
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,799
Did you send your letters?

61
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,759
Lord Valens.

62
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:34,799
My cousin in Teselya established
an army of barbarians.

63
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,799
They are coming.

64
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,599
What about you, Commander Seth?

65
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:42,318
My friends in Vidin answered my letter.

66
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:46,439
The armies are established, Lord
Valens, they^re coming to feed with blood.

67
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,399
Good.

68
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:54,519
Even if we burn down Osman's tribe..

69
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,839
...even if we stop the help
coming to him...

70
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:00,279
...we know that he won't stop.

71
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:03,439
The only way to stop him...

72
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:06,119
...is to cut off his head.

73
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,039
We will do that.

74
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:16,839
We will establish a base in Kartalgozu to
welcome the armies.

75
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,239
This duty is yours.

76
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,959
What will Osman's next target be?

77
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:28,319
If we know that, it will be
easy to cut off his head.

78
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,039
I'm listening.

79
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:36,839
If he moves towards
Kestel Castle...

80
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,839
...it'll be the end of him.

81
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:41,839
My soldiers are waiting in Lefke.

82
00:09:47,280 --> 00:09:49,119
Byzantine’s great commanders.

83
00:09:50,440 --> 00:09:55,519
What will Osman's next target be?

84
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:00,639
When I look at Osman's
previous conquests...

85
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:02,639
..the map shows that..

86
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:06,799
...he wants to cut contact
between Marmara and Bursa.

87
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,799
You're a real soldier.

88
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,999
Kopruhisar...

89
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,319
...is where he gets closer to his goal.

90
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:31,359
He wants to do this and rid
Anatolia of the Byzantines.

91
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,639
That's why his next goal...

92
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:37,719
...will be Koyunhisar.

93
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:39,959
If he takes control of it...

94
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:42,359
...İznik and Bursa will lose contact.

95
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:48,119
Byzantine’s great commanders...

96
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,919
and Lords...

97
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:56,559
You will take precaution in your castles.

98
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:59,759
Council brothers.

99
00:11:00,680 --> 00:11:02,519
Gather all of your soldiers.

100
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:07,039
Commander Milos.

101
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,399
Commander Seth.

102
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,959
When the armies arrive..

103
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,879
...not a single Turk will
breathe in this land.

104
00:11:24,200 --> 00:11:26,959
It's not enough to make an agreement.

105
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,279
We'll swear on Jesus Christ.

106
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:33,999
Priest.

107
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:12,599
Until we rest under the flag
of Jesus Christ.

108
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:18,919
We'll burn the infidels with the God’s sun.

109
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,679
Until heaven is ours.

110
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,519
Until heaven is ours,

111
00:12:24,520 --> 00:12:30,319
We'll make them go through hell.

112
00:12:31,760 --> 00:12:41,439
This is our oath.

113
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,719
Salam Alaikum.

114
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,439
Alaikum Salam, Osman Bey.

115
00:13:15,600 --> 00:13:16,919
Thank you.

116
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:18,919
Have a seat, Osman Bey.

117
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:31,879
Congratulations on the Kopruhisar
conquest, Osman Bey.

118
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:33,879
Thanks.

119
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,879
Thanks to you...

120
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,999
...we knew the location of all passages.

121
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,319
Thank you.

122
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,519
Where's your next target, Osman Bey?

123
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:48,879
Our target will aIways be Red Apple.

124
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,439
But...

125
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,119
...our short term goal...

126
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,839
...is for Byzantines...

127
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:59,679
..to leave the board.

128
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,679
It will be a tough battle.

129
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:07,719
We never deal with with the easy way.

130
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,799
Let Byzantines send an army.

131
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,759
We'll kill them all with our steel hands.

132
00:14:19,520 --> 00:14:21,319
They'll never stop Osman Bey.

133
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:23,559
This is a war between right and wrong.

134
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:27,159
They'll never stop even if you do.

135
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,629
But...

136
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:34,639
...you can never make
peace with superstitious beliefs.

137
00:14:34,880 --> 00:14:36,959
Stopping on the other hand..

138
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:39,079
...will only send us back.

139
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,959
Now tell me.

140
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:45,799
Let us know what you know.

141
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:50,359
Who is coming?

142
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:52,159
Lord Valens...

143
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:55,799
...has called for everyone who is
capable of holding a sword under his rule.

144
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,799
Especially...

145
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:00,719
...two cruel commanders.

146
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:05,479
His hands are covered with thousands
of brave men’s blood.

147
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:10,159
We'll cut off those
hands covered in blood.

148
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,359
But...

149
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:14,199
...if you tell me to behead
those who are..

150
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:17,359
...leading the army...

151
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,799
...that's okay too.

152
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:44,839
Commanders are fine.

153
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,359
What about the others?

154
00:15:48,360 --> 00:15:50,799
Men from Lord's own team.

155
00:15:50,800 --> 00:15:55,079
Those in the council are
always hidden as a precaution.

156
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:56,839
But...

157
00:15:56,840 --> 00:16:00,119
...you're the ones who
keep secrets within secrets.

158
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:03,039
There's no one who's
better at hiding than you.

159
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:04,559
Tell me.

160
00:16:04,560 --> 00:16:07,119
How can they hide from you?

161
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:12,679
There's no hidden or clear, Osman Bey.

162
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:14,639
There's no politics now.

163
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:18,119
There will be a war now.

164
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:20,239
Without the armies.

165
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:22,759
Without the big alliance being made.

166
00:16:27,760 --> 00:16:30,199
So, you're saying it’s hunting season, huh?

167
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,479
For Gokboru, it is time to hunt.

168
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:46,039
We will drown those who are...

169
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,559
...coming to kill us in their own blood.

170
00:16:48,560 --> 00:16:51,399
I will hunt Valens and those who stand with him...

171
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:54,599
down one by one.

172
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:56,999
And Koyunhisar...

173
00:16:57,600 --> 00:17:00,239
...will be my hunting ground.

174
00:17:03,160 --> 00:17:04,877
Don't worry.

175
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,079
I'm going to end them all.

176
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:15,919
Thank you.

177
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:18,519
- Thanks, Osman Bey.
- Thanks.

178
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,999
The dark midwife?

179
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:52,199
Alcicek, good news.

180
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:54,199
You're pregnant.

181
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:03,159
Are you serious, dark midwife?

182
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:05,719
Am I going to be a mother now?

183
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,079
Yes.

184
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:09,589
And Aktemur, a father?

185
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:11,119
Inshallah.

186
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:13,479
Mashallah, Alcicek.

187
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,959
When Aktemur hears about this...

188
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,479
Allah...

189
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:22,079
I hope this is good news, Inshallah.

190
00:18:22,080 --> 00:18:24,239
Alcicek, are you okay?

191
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,199
It is good news Malhun Hatun, it is.

192
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,839
Alcicek is pregnant.

193
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,439
The babies are coming one
after the other thank Allah.

194
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:43,519
Alcicek, I'm so happy to hear that.

195
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:46,199
May Allah allow you
to hold them in your arms.

196
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:48,279
- Amin.
- Amin, Inshallah.

197
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:51,119
Thank you.

198
00:18:51,120 --> 00:18:52,999
I need to go to the tribe now.

199
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,639
They are waiting for material for the burnt tents.

200
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:58,919
And I need to give the good news
to Aktemur and my mother.

201
00:18:58,920 --> 00:18:59,999
Of course.

202
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,559
But you can't go alone.
I'll send a few Alps with you.

203
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:04,559
No need, aunt Malhun.

204
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,679
Alps are waiting for me in the field.

205
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:09,439
It's okay to be safe.

206
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,439
Gorkluce.

207
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:01,319
My sons.

208
00:20:04,070 --> 00:20:05,909
Alps.

209
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:08,639
It's time for us to begin the conquest.

210
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:14,439
Our target is Koyunhisar.

211
00:20:21,320 --> 00:20:25,279
Kopruhisar gave us
control over the Iznik road.

212
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:31,839
Inshallah, the conquest of Koyunhisar, will
give us control over Bursa road.

213
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:36,039
Inshallah.

214
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:39,919
Inshallah, my Bey, but we could have
sent spies there if you told us.

215
00:20:40,880 --> 00:20:45,519
Where is our spy, Aktemur?

216
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:48,879
He might be here any minute, my Bey.

217
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:01,039
I told Aktemur once...

218
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:05,559
...and we had a spy in Koyunhisar
the whole time.

219
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:08,519
My Bey.

220
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:12,679
Have you been planning
to get Koyunhisar...

221
00:21:13,240 --> 00:21:16,079
...before even getting
Kopruhisar, my Bey?

222
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:21,719
If you knew about the things I
planned and dreamt of...

223
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,639
...you would never be able
to sleep at night.

224
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:27,929
Thanks.

225
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:33,759
Tell me, Kutlu.

226
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:38,759
They're happy after the damage
we suffered, my Bey.

227
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,319
They were planning to have fun...

228
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:45,159
...but Kopruhisar’s
conquest destroyed them.

229
00:21:45,640 --> 00:21:50,719
They moved all soldiers in nearby
castles and villages to Koyunhisar.

230
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,759
Lord must have arrived to Bursa.

231
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:55,399
They're waiting for us, my Bey.

232
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:59,479
Here are the maps, my Bey.

233
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:08,839
Let them wait.

234
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,959
Let them wait.

235
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:15,399
They will be afraid.

236
00:22:17,760 --> 00:22:21,719
They won't even be able to sleep at night;

237
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:25,759
They will be destroyed...

238
00:22:31,480 --> 00:22:35,119
...and when they’re least expecting it...

239
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:42,039
..Koyunhisar will become a property of Turks.

240
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:48,159
But there's something else
we have to do before.

241
00:22:49,560 --> 00:22:55,359
Some of them want to unite and kill us.

242
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:59,759
We'll march on them first.

243
00:23:05,629 --> 00:23:06,629
My Bey.

244
00:23:11,720 --> 00:23:14,229
We have news from our scouts.

245
00:23:14,279 --> 00:23:17,918
Esrigun Hatun is going to Yenisehir.

246
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:28,519
Alps.

247
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,279
We're going to Yenisehir.

248
00:23:46,560 --> 00:23:48,919
May it be easy.

249
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:58,439
- May it be easy.
- Thanks.

250
00:24:04,870 --> 00:24:08,229
- May I?
- It's halal, go ahead.

251
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:23,039
- May it be easy.
- Thank you. Welcome.

252
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:25,399
Thank you.

253
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:40,639
It's silk, huh?

254
00:24:43,280 --> 00:24:46,199
- Is it good?
- It's the best.

255
00:24:46,480 --> 00:24:50,159
Thanks to Osman Bey, all goods
in Yenisehir are good.

256
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:54,899
So, Osman Bey is taking good care of you.

257
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:57,919
How are the merchants doing?

258
00:24:58,920 --> 00:25:03,359
He does not stop fighting, and he
always keeps our well-being in his mind.

259
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,439
He always protects us.

260
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:09,599
He protects the merchants, may
Allah bless Osman Bey.

261
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:15,239
You keep complimenting him, but...

262
00:25:15,840 --> 00:25:19,759
- that's not what I've heard.
- What did you hear, Hatun?

263
00:25:27,840 --> 00:25:31,279
Tell me, what did you hear about Osman Bey?

264
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:36,079
I heard that he is a dreamer.

265
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:41,959
He dreams things that are beyond him.

266
00:25:42,760 --> 00:25:45,639
It looks like you've
heard these from the enemy.

267
00:25:46,600 --> 00:25:49,039
Don't believe everything you hear.

268
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:51,839
Is what I heard a lie, Hatun?

269
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:56,439
Isn't Osman Bey putting a heavy
burden upon his people with his dreams?

270
00:25:57,040 --> 00:26:00,399
What is the dream that
becomes a burden to the people?

271
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:05,919
The rebel called Nayman on one hand
and Bursa Lord on the other.

272
00:26:06,160 --> 00:26:09,599
And there is also Konya.
You lose everyday.

273
00:26:09,760 --> 00:26:12,959
You are bleeding, but you keep fighting.

274
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:15,199
You are crossing the line, Hatun.

275
00:26:16,080 --> 00:26:18,599
Your ignorance must be leading
you talk bravely like this.

276
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:22,079
I don't know where you are coming
from, but these are the borderlands.

277
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:26,199
Wherever you go, you face
an enemy in these lands!

278
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:30,439
You will learn where my bravery comes
from when we are introduced.

279
00:26:33,080 --> 00:26:34,999
You are Esrigun hatun.

280
00:26:37,680 --> 00:26:39,879
You must be Malhun Hatun.

281
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:44,439
Then what are you doing here? We
were waiting for you at the mansion.

282
00:26:45,600 --> 00:26:49,879
I wanted to learn about the
people’s opinion on Osman Bey.

283
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,239
As you know...

284
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,799
...you are bound to Seljuk state...

285
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:00,839
...and Seljuk state is bound to us.

286
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:11,279
Sultan Alaeddin's secret house.

287
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:14,479
Celali.

288
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:18,159
Send messengers all around Seljuk state.

289
00:27:18,600 --> 00:27:21,069
I will take my throne back!

290
00:27:23,640 --> 00:27:26,839
I want soldiers loyal to me behind me!

291
00:27:41,760 --> 00:27:43,559
Your command, my Sultan.

292
00:27:56,080 --> 00:27:58,839
When our soldiers arrive
at the borderlands...

293
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:02,719
..we will take revenge from
those who dethroned you!

294
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:08,639
I swear that we will kill all of them!

295
00:28:08,960 --> 00:28:11,239
Those who lived with my mercy...

296
00:28:11,880 --> 00:28:14,079
...will soon live with my wrath.

297
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:20,959
I will ask soldiers from Lord
and Nayman for the army we will gather.

298
00:28:25,960 --> 00:28:29,279
Lord pledged his friendship to Sultan Mesut.

299
00:28:32,040 --> 00:28:34,319
And Nayman will support him.

300
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:41,079
We will build our victory with
our own hands, my Sultan!

301
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:45,559
Then, the rebellious borderlands...

302
00:28:46,040 --> 00:28:50,519
...and Osman will be killed by us!

303
00:28:52,240 --> 00:28:55,479
No children of Osman will...

304
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:59,559
...sit on the throne, and they will not have a future!

305
00:29:03,800 --> 00:29:05,559
But first...

306
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:09,199
...I will punish these traitors.

307
00:29:10,560 --> 00:29:14,759
Bengi and Alcicek survived the
attack on the tribe.

308
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,519
Karabul is after them.

309
00:29:19,800 --> 00:29:22,119
When he brings Alcicek...

310
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:26,079
...I will punish Bengi and Alcicek...

311
00:29:26,760 --> 00:29:29,079
..with my own hands.

312
00:30:02,320 --> 00:30:04,359
Mother Sultan wants her alive.

313
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:15,439
Alps! It's a trap!

314
00:30:17,200 --> 00:30:19,719
Alps! Protect Alcicek Hatun!

315
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,239
Come on!
Attack!

316
00:30:57,760 --> 00:30:59,439
No way out.

317
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:01,399
Mother Sultan is waiting for you.

318
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:05,719
Your mother and you will
pay for your treason.

319
00:31:05,720 --> 00:31:07,719
There's no way out.
Surrender.

320
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:09,399
You're the traitor.

321
00:31:09,440 --> 00:31:11,439
Ismihan is the traitor.

322
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:13,439
Both you and you mother will die.

323
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,679
Hurry! Follow her!

324
00:32:07,000 --> 00:32:08,239
Osman Bey, welcome.

325
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:11,799
May Allah bless you, Osman Bey.

326
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:15,119
Thank you.

327
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:21,159
May Allah protect you, my Bey.

328
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:37,679
Long live, Osman Bey

329
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:52,959
This way!
Follow her.

330
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:54,799
Come on.

331
00:32:56,360 --> 00:32:57,679
Hurry! Come on.

332
00:33:00,360 --> 00:33:01,959
Over here!
Come on.

333
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:13,439
Come on.

334
00:35:05,760 --> 00:35:07,639
She went this way.

335
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:09,679
She's injured.

336
00:35:09,680 --> 00:35:12,439
She couldn’t have made it far.

337
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,679
My baby.

338
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:55,479
She got away.

339
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:57,719
We're going back.

340
00:35:57,720 --> 00:35:59,999
We'll go by the riverbed.

341
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:16,479
She is not here.

342
00:37:18,520 --> 00:37:20,119
We're going back.

343
00:37:20,120 --> 00:37:23,519
What will we tell Mother Sultan now?

344
00:37:28,640 --> 00:37:30,759
She's injured.

345
00:37:31,880 --> 00:37:33,439
She won't make it alive
out of here.

346
00:37:33,440 --> 00:37:34,959
Come on.

347
00:38:26,120 --> 00:38:29,039
They took Alcicek Hatun.

348
00:38:29,560 --> 00:38:30,719
Alps...

349
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,679
Gather around.

350
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:55,679
Leave no trace behind.

351
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:04,879
Bring my horse.

352
00:39:10,360 --> 00:39:13,199
I'm going to let Mother Sultan know.

353
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:38,399
Welcome to our mansion, Esrigun Hatun.

354
00:39:38,640 --> 00:39:43,319
If you are our guest
until we get Ismihan...

355
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:46,119
..then, you will be hosted
without any mistakes.

356
00:39:46,120 --> 00:39:50,919
They prison us between stone walls.

357
00:39:51,240 --> 00:39:53,919
You must have fallen for that as well...

358
00:39:54,320 --> 00:39:58,719
..and abandoned your tents.

359
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:12,599
Do you think sycamores forget
about their roots...

360
00:40:13,680 --> 00:40:17,399
...as they grow
towards the sky, Hatun?

361
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:21,639
I don't know about you...

362
00:40:21,720 --> 00:40:25,199
...but both our mansions and tents...

363
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:29,359
...are filled with hearts
beating for the Word of Allah.

364
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:32,519
Is that a girl?

365
00:40:33,080 --> 00:40:35,799
She's pretty, too.

366
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:40,439
Although Turkmens live in separated locations...

367
00:40:41,080 --> 00:40:43,599
...their cause is the same.

368
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:49,319
Do you think Cerkutay knows her?

369
00:40:49,800 --> 00:40:53,039
That's the difference between
Turkmens and us.

370
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:57,879
We conquer more lands while
you only dream about it.

371
00:40:58,880 --> 00:41:00,559
Well...

372
00:41:00,960 --> 00:41:04,439
...if we only spoke and
didn’t take any action...

373
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:08,719
...you wouldn't be
here now, Esrigun Hatun.

374
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:14,439
You must be aware of the struggle
you went through so I’d be here...

375
00:41:14,640 --> 00:41:18,639
..and what would have happened if I
refused to do so, Osman Bey.

376
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:21,199
You're right.

377
00:41:21,480 --> 00:41:23,719
You're right, thank you.

378
00:41:24,040 --> 00:41:29,119
You helped us make it out of the trap
that they had set.

379
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:32,159
Thank you.

380
00:41:43,520 --> 00:41:46,839
Sultan Mesut is on the throne.

381
00:41:48,240 --> 00:41:52,039
Muslims are brothers
and that’s what happened.

382
00:41:52,920 --> 00:41:56,959
We will do our part, as it needed.

383
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:03,239
If we don't kill and die for
the world of Islam...

384
00:42:03,560 --> 00:42:08,919
...the blood Nayman spilled
will stain the flag of Tabriz.

385
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:13,799
Both you and Gazhan Khan
are aware of that.

386
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:27,079
Anyway, we can talk about it later.

387
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:32,039
Prepare a nice dinner tonight so that we can share...

388
00:42:32,400 --> 00:42:34,319
...our bread...

389
00:42:34,640 --> 00:42:36,559
...our problems...

390
00:42:36,640 --> 00:42:38,559
...and our call with our guest.

391
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:44,639
To share a call, you must first
share bread, Osman Bey.

392
00:42:45,320 --> 00:42:46,719
I'd be glad.

393
00:42:47,000 --> 00:42:49,559
Thanks.

394
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:53,799
Aktemur...

395
00:42:55,360 --> 00:42:57,079
...you should stay, as well.

396
00:42:58,080 --> 00:43:01,679
Tell the Alps to bring Alcicek here.

397
00:43:22,360 --> 00:43:24,919
We'll recover from this, Inshallah.

398
00:43:25,600 --> 00:43:27,279
Inshallah.

399
00:43:27,280 --> 00:43:29,039
Bengi Hatun.

400
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:30,959
Bengi Hatun...

401
00:43:31,080 --> 00:43:34,639
...Osman Bey disregarded your
exile sentence.

402
00:43:38,160 --> 00:43:39,879
Thanks.

403
00:43:40,360 --> 00:43:42,959
But no crime should go unpunished.

404
00:43:43,160 --> 00:43:47,559
I'll gladly accept any punishment
once my tribe is doing better.

405
00:43:49,400 --> 00:43:53,239
The supply needed for the tents
haven't arrived yet.

406
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:56,039
What should we do?

407
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,999
Alcicek is late.

408
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,519
She knew that we wee in a hurry.

409
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:09,359
Aybars, send an Alp.

410
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:30,199
Are you okay?

411
00:44:31,640 --> 00:44:33,079
Get the healer here.

412
00:44:33,240 --> 00:44:35,999
What happened?
Who did this to you?

413
00:44:37,040 --> 00:44:39,099
Bengi Hatun.

414
00:44:39,400 --> 00:44:41,039
Bengi Hatun...

415
00:44:41,200 --> 00:44:43,119
Alcicek Hatun was kidnapped.

416
00:44:43,280 --> 00:44:45,039
By whom?

417
00:44:45,640 --> 00:44:46,999
The Mother...

418
00:44:47,120 --> 00:44:49,839
They mentioned the Mother Sultan.

419
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,399
Ismihan...

420
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:57,959
Alcicek!

421
00:44:58,400 --> 00:45:00,639
Calm down, Bengi Hatun.

422
00:45:00,800 --> 00:45:03,799
Don't think of bad things!
We will find Alcicek.

423
00:45:04,320 --> 00:45:07,279
Alps! Bring the spies!

424
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:10,129
Make preparations, we will
go to Yenisehir, come on;

425
00:45:10,240 --> 00:45:12,279
Call the healer!

426
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:15,159
Come on.

427
00:45:16,560 --> 00:45:25,359
Sultan Alaeddin's secret house.

428
00:45:42,400 --> 00:45:43,439
Alcicek.

429
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:48,079
Where is she?

430
00:45:48,800 --> 00:45:50,319
I was about to capture her...

431
00:45:55,320 --> 00:45:57,479
You were about to capture her?

432
00:46:03,400 --> 00:46:06,639
This bloodied cape and
her sword.

433
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:11,159
I lost her track in the forest.
It is impossible for her to survive.

434
00:46:11,360 --> 00:46:12,519
She is wounded.

435
00:46:13,520 --> 00:46:16,559
You couldn't do one thing!

436
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,959
What will we do now, madam?

437
00:46:25,640 --> 00:46:27,679
Did anyone see Alcicek?

438
00:46:29,400 --> 00:46:30,599
No.

439
00:46:31,120 --> 00:46:33,319
She was distant from the Alps.

440
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:36,479
We cleaned the tracks and
removed the dead bodies.

441
00:46:37,160 --> 00:46:39,719
Then, we will continue our plan.

442
00:46:41,080 --> 00:46:43,679
Since no one has seen Alcicek..

443
00:46:44,040 --> 00:46:47,079
...then they won’t be
able to find her corpse.

444
00:46:47,360 --> 00:46:51,079
They will think that I have Alcicek.

445
00:46:51,880 --> 00:46:56,319
We will send word to Bengi, if she
does not come to where we want...

446
00:46:57,680 --> 00:47:00,959
...she will be sure that
I will kill her daughter.

447
00:47:02,920 --> 00:47:04,639
What if she does not come, madam?

448
00:47:05,920 --> 00:47:08,159
Motherhood...

449
00:47:08,760 --> 00:47:10,199
Motherhood...

450
00:47:12,480 --> 00:47:16,279
...can bury you alive.

451
00:47:17,920 --> 00:47:21,399
When Bengi sees that her daughter's
scent is mixed with blood...

452
00:47:21,920 --> 00:47:24,559
..she will come to me.

453
00:47:29,160 --> 00:47:31,279
Yenisehir, Osman Bey's mansion.

454
00:48:01,360 --> 00:48:03,119
What are they talking about?

455
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:05,399
I don't know.

456
00:48:05,400 --> 00:48:07,239
They are whispering.

457
00:48:15,160 --> 00:48:16,639
Gurbuz.

458
00:48:19,520 --> 00:48:20,839
Alp...

459
00:48:33,400 --> 00:48:35,799
So, you are here, huh, Cerkutay Alp?

460
00:48:39,640 --> 00:48:46,599
Gurbuz Alp told me everything one by one.

461
00:48:50,840 --> 00:48:52,279
What did he tell you?

462
00:48:52,520 --> 00:48:54,039
What did you tell her?

463
00:48:56,880 --> 00:49:00,399
Well, I told her everything.

464
00:49:07,000 --> 00:49:09,839
You must be really brave, Cerkutay..

465
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:17,759
You are brave enough to ask for
her hand in marriage.

466
00:49:20,720 --> 00:49:22,799
What are you saying, mother?

467
00:49:23,360 --> 00:49:24,839
Shut up!

468
00:49:25,120 --> 00:49:27,439
We will talk later.

469
00:49:34,560 --> 00:49:37,719
Cerkutay, so, you are..

470
00:49:38,640 --> 00:49:41,759
...in love with my...

471
00:49:42,480 --> 00:49:45,039
...daughter, huh?

472
00:49:55,280 --> 00:49:57,999
I won't let my daughter
marry a crazy person.

473
00:50:00,600 --> 00:50:03,599
I said what I said but...

474
00:50:04,480 --> 00:50:06,079
...Gurbuz Alp said...

475
00:50:09,080 --> 00:50:10,959
..."he is smart."

476
00:50:10,960 --> 00:50:13,719
He said, "That's why he seems crazy."

477
00:50:24,120 --> 00:50:26,559
You're a good swordsman.

478
00:50:26,560 --> 00:50:28,319
I asked around about you.

479
00:50:28,920 --> 00:50:32,439
There is no better son in law than you.

480
00:50:37,120 --> 00:50:38,679
But...

481
00:50:39,320 --> 00:50:41,119
...I have 3 conditions.

482
00:50:42,360 --> 00:50:44,959
I accept them.

483
00:50:48,120 --> 00:50:49,319
Wait!

484
00:50:50,400 --> 00:50:51,959
Listen.

485
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:56,639
When you marry my girl...

486
00:50:56,640 --> 00:50:57,959
Yes.

487
00:50:59,360 --> 00:51:01,639
Where will you live?

488
00:51:06,560 --> 00:51:07,559
The mansion.

489
00:51:07,560 --> 00:51:08,599
No.

490
00:51:09,040 --> 00:51:11,279
First, I want a house!

491
00:51:13,360 --> 00:51:14,719
Of course.

492
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:17,079
We'll get a house, Cerkutay.

493
00:51:25,240 --> 00:51:27,999
You'll pay mahr which will be...

494
00:51:28,520 --> 00:51:29,999
...Ulgen's weight in gold.

495
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:41,719
Of course.

496
00:51:42,480 --> 00:51:44,439
We'll get it, right, Cerkutay?

497
00:51:52,960 --> 00:51:55,839
I want...

498
00:51:55,840 --> 00:51:58,719
the biggest greatest gift.

499
00:51:59,240 --> 00:52:01,199
It will be this height.

500
00:52:04,120 --> 00:52:05,439
Of course.

501
00:52:06,120 --> 00:52:08,359
We'll get it, right, Cerkutay?

502
00:52:11,680 --> 00:52:14,119
Yes.
Find those first.

503
00:52:15,040 --> 00:52:18,079
Then come and ask for my
daughter's hand in marriage.

504
00:52:18,080 --> 00:52:20,079
Off you go.
Go on.

505
00:52:20,080 --> 00:52:21,879
- Let's go.
- Go.

506
00:52:21,880 --> 00:52:23,879
Let's go.
Let’s go.

507
00:52:30,360 --> 00:52:31,319
Mother.

508
00:52:32,120 --> 00:52:35,359
Why didn't you ask for more?

509
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:37,239
Ask him to give us Yenisehir.

510
00:52:37,360 --> 00:52:40,759
Or better yet, ask to have the
city where it all started.

511
00:52:40,760 --> 00:52:42,239
Maybe, Inegol?

512
00:52:42,680 --> 00:52:44,119
Ulgen.

513
00:52:44,200 --> 00:52:46,119
How can he find all of that?

514
00:52:46,120 --> 00:52:47,359
Ulgen!

515
00:52:47,840 --> 00:52:50,279
I have just one daughter.

516
00:52:50,280 --> 00:52:52,639
It's not easy to marry my
daughter.

517
00:52:55,880 --> 00:52:57,039
He must do it.

518
00:53:13,400 --> 00:53:14,239
Mother.

519
00:53:14,840 --> 00:53:15,799
Aunt.

520
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:18,359
Alcicek's not here.

521
00:53:18,760 --> 00:53:20,039
Did you hear from her?

522
00:53:20,040 --> 00:53:21,639
No, son.

523
00:53:21,840 --> 00:53:24,159
We have
sent a messenger but he hasn’t arrived.

524
00:53:24,160 --> 00:53:25,799
I'm worried too.

525
00:53:27,960 --> 00:53:29,959
Where are you, Alcicek?

526
00:53:30,200 --> 00:53:31,959
She said she had good news.

527
00:53:34,480 --> 00:53:35,479
What?

528
00:53:36,520 --> 00:53:38,879
It's good news, Ayse, but...

529
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:40,439
..it’s a secret for now.

530
00:53:42,000 --> 00:53:44,879
Attention!
Osman Bey is coming!

531
00:54:01,400 --> 00:54:02,919
Salam Alaikum.

532
00:54:03,720 --> 00:54:05,599
Alaikum Salam, my Bey.

533
00:54:15,720 --> 00:54:17,159
Have a seat.

534
00:54:30,840 --> 00:54:33,559
"In the name of Allah, the Most
Gracious, the Most Merciful."

535
00:54:34,000 --> 00:54:35,999
Go ahead.
Enjoy your meal.

536
00:54:56,760 --> 00:54:59,679
You accepted our invite.

537
00:54:59,960 --> 00:55:02,399
Thank you.

538
00:55:03,560 --> 00:55:05,879
We shared our bread.

539
00:55:05,880 --> 00:55:07,919
And now it's time to...

540
00:55:07,920 --> 00:55:11,799
...share our worries and call.

541
00:55:12,240 --> 00:55:13,879
So......

542
00:55:13,880 --> 00:55:16,319
40 foxes...

543
00:55:16,320 --> 00:55:19,119
...walk around these borders...

544
00:55:19,120 --> 00:55:23,039
...and every one of their tails
touch one and another.

545
00:55:23,040 --> 00:55:26,839
We try to solve the problems
caused by this.

546
00:55:27,320 --> 00:55:30,159
I see it, Osman
Bey, I see it.

547
00:55:30,160 --> 00:55:33,599
And the biggest fox is Lord Valens.

548
00:55:33,600 --> 00:55:37,639
He thinks that he can move
every stone on these lands...

549
00:55:37,640 --> 00:55:42,519
...since he went to visit Sultan
Mesut when he was crowned.

550
00:55:43,280 --> 00:55:45,119
I know that.

551
00:55:45,120 --> 00:55:46,919
I know.

552
00:55:46,920 --> 00:55:50,679
He sent his regards.

553
00:55:51,440 --> 00:55:53,399
Lord Valens...

554
00:55:54,120 --> 00:55:56,279
..eats with the wolf...

555
00:55:56,280 --> 00:55:58,719
...and cries with the shepherd.

556
00:56:00,920 --> 00:56:02,519
That's his nature.

557
00:56:02,520 --> 00:56:04,959
He always talks behind people’s back.

558
00:56:04,960 --> 00:56:08,039
That's why he has a
lot of people with him.

559
00:56:08,040 --> 00:56:10,399
He has a lot of allies.

560
00:56:10,400 --> 00:56:12,159
Even...

561
00:56:12,160 --> 00:56:17,159
...he has many people who
would die for him.

562
00:56:17,800 --> 00:56:21,199
As long as Nayman with the Lord...

563
00:56:21,960 --> 00:56:24,759
...it's hard to defeat
them both.

564
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:28,119
Wherever the Lord stands...

565
00:56:28,120 --> 00:56:32,719
I will cut that traitor
Nayman’s liver off of his body.

566
00:56:33,640 --> 00:56:38,279
We will take the mountains Lord
Valens gets support from.

567
00:56:38,560 --> 00:56:41,399
After we leave him without power...

568
00:56:42,800 --> 00:56:46,079
...Nayman will fall into our hands.

569
00:56:46,480 --> 00:56:49,239
What do you have in mind, Osman Bey?

570
00:56:49,560 --> 00:56:52,879
You will learn about it like
everyone else, Esrigun Hatun.

571
00:57:00,680 --> 00:57:07,889
We saved his life but he doesn't trust us.

572
00:57:08,020 --> 00:57:12,999
Don t take it personally, Esrigun
Hatun but a Bey's business is secret.

573
00:57:22,160 --> 00:57:24,119
Thanks.

574
00:57:27,640 --> 00:57:29,719
Thanks, Osman Bey.

575
00:57:29,720 --> 00:57:30,719
Mashallah.

576
00:57:30,720 --> 00:57:35,479
It can be seen that you raised your
sons for the world of Islam.

577
00:57:35,480 --> 00:57:40,559
Someone who is no stranger to our
language has a place in our hearts.

578
00:57:41,320 --> 00:57:46,679
The wind and the storm of the Islam world...

579
00:57:46,680 --> 00:57:49,359
..will never end.

580
00:57:49,360 --> 00:57:51,199
But the enemies...

581
00:57:51,200 --> 00:57:54,479
...think that the storm will put out our fire.

582
00:57:55,280 --> 00:57:56,239
But...

583
00:57:57,200 --> 00:57:59,759
...it only strengthens us.

584
00:58:00,800 --> 00:58:02,199
So...

585
00:58:02,200 --> 00:58:05,719
..a seed of the flower which
grows on these lands....

586
00:58:05,720 --> 00:58:09,639
...will travel all over the world.

587
00:58:10,480 --> 00:58:13,199
And that's what unites us.

588
00:58:15,040 --> 00:58:16,719
To unite..

589
00:58:16,720 --> 00:58:19,199
...we need to know each other well.

590
00:58:19,200 --> 00:58:21,279
We need to get to know each other well.

591
00:58:23,840 --> 00:58:26,079
And our sons...

592
00:58:26,760 --> 00:58:29,279
...were brought up with the same idea.

593
00:58:29,960 --> 00:58:33,919
They were taught by my Sheykh Edebali....

594
00:58:33,920 --> 00:58:35,159
...and now...

595
00:58:36,400 --> 00:58:39,159
...they're entrusted to Kumral AbdaI.

596
00:58:41,160 --> 00:58:42,439
Thank Allah...

597
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:47,239
...Allah gifted me with this mission.

598
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:50,799
Our only worry and mission..

599
00:58:50,800 --> 00:58:52,919
...is to hold on to the rope of Allah.

600
00:58:52,920 --> 00:58:56,559
And raise our children to do so too.

601
00:58:59,080 --> 00:59:02,439
What does it say in the verse of the Quran?

602
00:59:02,880 --> 00:59:06,999
"And hold firmly to the rope of Allah..

603
00:59:08,160 --> 00:59:10,079
...all together and do not become divided."
[3:103]

604
00:59:10,080 --> 00:59:13,759
Whenever I hear this,
it shakes me Kumral Abdal

605
00:59:14,440 --> 00:59:16,959
What do we take from it?

606
00:59:16,960 --> 00:59:20,599
Allah says that...

607
00:59:20,600 --> 00:59:24,639
...Allah's rope is a rope hanging down
from the sky down to earth.

608
00:59:24,640 --> 00:59:28,479
Of course we can not look for this rope with our eyes.

609
00:59:28,480 --> 00:59:30,879
We can see it with the eyes of our hearts.

610
00:59:31,760 --> 00:59:34,719
We know that this rope...

611
00:59:34,720 --> 00:59:37,319
...is Quran and Islam.

612
00:59:37,840 --> 00:59:39,679
It's the mission of Islam.

613
00:59:58,840 --> 01:00:01,959
Why are we still waiting, mother?

614
01:00:02,600 --> 01:00:04,479
Every minute spent here is wasted.

615
01:00:05,080 --> 01:00:09,119
We're supposed to prepare an army
but you're messing with Bengi.

616
01:00:10,640 --> 01:00:13,199
The Mother Sultan of Seljuk...

617
01:00:13,360 --> 01:00:16,799
...does not leave any unfinished business.

618
01:00:19,600 --> 01:00:26,239
She never forgives a
pawn like Bengi.

619
01:00:27,160 --> 01:00:29,839
I will take back everything...

620
01:00:30,160 --> 01:00:33,999
...that they stole from us.

621
01:00:37,440 --> 01:00:41,199
But I’ll get my revenge first.

622
01:00:47,840 --> 01:00:51,159
Bengi will scream in pain.

623
01:00:51,880 --> 01:00:54,319
I will watch her die.

624
01:00:55,280 --> 01:00:58,479
The end I have prepared for her..

625
01:00:59,000 --> 01:01:01,759
...will be spoken about for centuries.

626
01:01:09,680 --> 01:01:11,439
Mother...

627
01:01:12,760 --> 01:01:15,159
...your ambition is going to get us in trouble.

628
01:01:16,040 --> 01:01:18,879
Ambition isn’t the reason, justice is!

629
01:01:19,400 --> 01:01:22,079
No one can cross me!

630
01:01:22,520 --> 01:01:26,039
and those who do pay for it!

631
01:01:27,080 --> 01:01:28,399
You'll see.

632
01:01:28,600 --> 01:01:31,519
Everyone will see!

633
01:01:46,600 --> 01:01:51,159
Just like how the stars are scattered
throughout the sky...

634
01:01:51,680 --> 01:01:54,999
...Muslims are scattered on the earth as well.

635
01:01:55,440 --> 01:02:01,239
It's not good when Muslims stay
that way like the stars do.

636
01:02:02,040 --> 01:02:08,079
When separated, Muslims can't overcome
the darkness of the infidels.

637
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:12,119
Separation is a Muslim's test.

638
01:02:12,920 --> 01:02:16,159
Quran is the most important guide...

639
01:02:16,320 --> 01:02:20,359
...Allah sent to help us get through the test.

640
01:02:21,320 --> 01:02:26,599
For that reason, Muslims shall
embrace the Great Quran together...

641
01:02:26,920 --> 01:02:30,799
..so that Allah's mercy..

642
01:02:30,960 --> 01:02:32,759
...can hug people.

643
01:02:33,960 --> 01:02:37,039
You spoke well, Kumral Abdal..

644
01:02:37,320 --> 01:02:41,279
..but even Muslims have nafs.

645
01:02:41,880 --> 01:02:48,199
Even though everything belongs to Allah,
they’re in a race to see who has more...

646
01:02:48,400 --> 01:02:51,559
...and since that's the case,
it's difficult to stay in Allah’s path...

647
01:02:52,080 --> 01:02:55,959
...after joining such a race.

648
01:02:58,520 --> 01:03:04,029
He says that "Surely the most noble of you in the sight
of Allah is the most righteous among you" [49:13]

649
01:03:04,520 --> 01:03:08,199
Those who are already in Allah's path...

650
01:03:08,960 --> 01:03:11,519
..shall overcome the test.

651
01:03:11,960 --> 01:03:14,039
They become a whole.

652
01:03:14,360 --> 01:03:19,439
They know that Islam is above
all races and all languages.

653
01:03:20,120 --> 01:03:26,199
Hearts that beat to spread
the Religion of Allah are one.

654
01:03:27,880 --> 01:03:32,159
Of course there will be hypocrites among you.

655
01:03:32,800 --> 01:03:37,999
There will be those who claim
that they share our cause but betray us.

656
01:03:39,120 --> 01:03:44,039
But Muslims protect and
stay true to each other.

657
01:03:45,160 --> 01:03:49,079
We will not let our guards down
against those...

658
01:03:49,280 --> 01:03:52,759
...who are waiting with daggers in their hands.

659
01:03:53,600 --> 01:03:58,119
May Allah allow us to remain united
against such hypocrites...

660
01:03:58,480 --> 01:04:00,279
...and remain strong.

661
01:04:04,480 --> 01:04:08,439
I hope you're among those
who stay true to each other, Osman Bey.

662
01:04:09,080 --> 01:04:11,439
For sure, Esrigun Hatun.

663
01:04:12,560 --> 01:04:16,799
We're true to both our enemies and friends.

664
01:04:17,960 --> 01:04:20,879
I see that's the case for you as well.

665
01:04:22,600 --> 01:04:25,399
May Allah keep you in his path.

666
01:04:25,680 --> 01:04:27,519
Amen.

667
01:04:35,800 --> 01:04:37,279
Osman!

668
01:04:37,640 --> 01:04:39,359
Aktemur!

669
01:04:39,640 --> 01:04:41,639
Bala!

670
01:04:49,680 --> 01:04:51,439
Osman!

671
01:04:51,960 --> 01:04:53,759
What's wrong?

672
01:04:54,160 --> 01:04:56,599
Tell me what happened.

673
01:04:56,760 --> 01:05:00,119
Mother... Where's Alcicek?

674
01:05:01,800 --> 01:05:05,599
Alcicek’ Ismihan kidnapped Alcicek.

675
01:05:05,920 --> 01:05:07,439
What?

676
01:05:09,880 --> 01:05:12,159
Mother’? Aunt?
How could this happen?

677
01:05:15,640 --> 01:05:17,439
Alcicek?

678
01:05:18,320 --> 01:05:20,199
Alcicek is pregnant.

679
01:05:24,880 --> 01:05:26,719
She was going to give you the good news.

680
01:05:27,600 --> 01:05:29,719
Pregnant?

681
01:05:32,040 --> 01:05:33,159
Mother?

682
01:05:34,400 --> 01:05:36,639
Am I going to be a father?

683
01:05:39,200 --> 01:05:40,679
How was she kidnapped?

684
01:05:40,680 --> 01:05:43,279
We checked everywhere,
there are no traces.

685
01:05:43,840 --> 01:05:49,159
We searched everywhere from the tribe to Yenisehir,
there is no trace of alps or Alcicek.

686
01:05:50,160 --> 01:05:52,119
The wounded alp that came here
became a martyr.

687
01:05:52,160 --> 01:05:54,319
We couldn't learn where they were ambushed.

688
01:05:59,080 --> 01:06:03,239
Alps!
You will search everywhere, come on!

689
01:06:05,200 --> 01:06:06,759
We are going to the assembly now.

690
01:06:08,840 --> 01:06:10,079
Don't worry.

691
01:06:10,520 --> 01:06:13,399
We will find your child and Alcicek.

692
01:06:13,800 --> 01:06:14,919
Come on.

693
01:06:17,640 --> 01:06:18,759
Come on.

694
01:06:41,400 --> 01:06:42,639
Mother.

695
01:06:47,280 --> 01:06:48,719
Mother, where are you?

696
01:06:56,920 --> 01:06:59,559
Oh Allah, help!

697
01:07:01,000 --> 01:07:02,879
Help me.

698
01:07:11,160 --> 01:07:14,599
I told you to stay at the tribe,
why are you here, nephew?

699
01:07:17,520 --> 01:07:19,239
Alps brought this.

700
01:07:19,840 --> 01:07:21,239
It's for you.

701
01:07:21,680 --> 01:07:24,359
It's personal, I wanted to bring it myself.

702
01:07:24,720 --> 01:07:27,119
They said no one but Bengi hatun should open it.

703
01:07:30,960 --> 01:07:36,039
If you want to see Alcicek alive,
come to Alatas, near Karaagac.

704
01:07:36,960 --> 01:07:38,639
You will come alone.

705
01:07:39,160 --> 01:07:41,799
If you tell anyone, you won't...

706
01:07:45,640 --> 01:07:48,079
...you won't see your child again.

707
01:07:51,360 --> 01:07:53,319
Ismihan!

708
01:07:55,560 --> 01:07:56,799
What is this!?

709
01:08:12,880 --> 01:08:14,719
Alcicek!

710
01:08:15,240 --> 01:08:17,238
Alcicek!

711
01:08:21,560 --> 01:08:22,879
I will come.

712
01:08:23,840 --> 01:08:25,158
I will come.

713
01:08:27,479 --> 01:08:29,719
I will save you my daughter.

714
01:08:30,960 --> 01:08:33,839
I will not leave you her!

715
01:08:36,880 --> 01:08:38,959
Be patient, daughter.

716
01:08:41,319 --> 01:08:43,158
I will save you and my grandchild.

717
01:08:44,960 --> 01:08:48,359
Aunt, this is a trap.

718
01:08:48,640 --> 01:08:52,559
If you go there alone, Ismihan will kill you.

719
01:08:54,720 --> 01:08:57,839
You will not say anything to anyone.

720
01:08:58,640 --> 01:09:01,759
My daughter's and grandchild’s lives depend on it.

721
01:09:01,760 --> 01:09:03,037
Never, Aybars!

722
01:09:04,200 --> 01:09:05,399
Never.

723
01:09:14,240 --> 01:09:17,479
The carriage left Yenisehir,
but there is no trace on the path.

724
01:09:17,600 --> 01:09:19,959
They must have cleaned it after the ambush.

725
01:09:19,960 --> 01:09:23,037
Ismihan wouldn't kidnap Alcicek without a reason.

726
01:09:23,479 --> 01:09:25,919
She will want something for sure.

727
01:09:29,160 --> 01:09:29,839
Boran.

728
01:09:29,840 --> 01:09:30,529
My Bey.

729
01:09:30,529 --> 01:09:32,198
Increase the number of Alps.

730
01:09:32,680 --> 01:09:35,078
You will search everywhere in the borderlands!

731
01:09:35,520 --> 01:09:36,599
As you command my Bey.

732
01:09:36,600 --> 01:09:37,308
Cerkutay.

733
01:09:37,308 --> 01:09:37,919
My Bey.

734
01:09:37,919 --> 01:09:39,959
You will take scouting alps with you.

735
01:09:40,240 --> 01:09:43,078
You will search everywhere from here to tribe.

736
01:09:45,920 --> 01:09:47,599
As you command my Bey.

737
01:09:48,160 --> 01:09:50,999
I have skilled scouts among my men.

738
01:09:52,160 --> 01:09:54,799
We would like to do our part.

739
01:09:58,880 --> 01:10:01,359
Thank you. Thank you.

740
01:10:01,840 --> 01:10:03,039
May I come in?

741
01:10:04,440 --> 01:10:05,399
Come in.

742
01:10:13,480 --> 01:10:14,919
Bengi Hatun.

743
01:10:15,160 --> 01:10:16,919
If Ismihan sends word to you..

744
01:10:18,160 --> 01:10:19,759
...tell us right away.

745
01:10:21,640 --> 01:10:23,399
What can she want from me?

746
01:10:23,800 --> 01:10:26,439
She took my beloved one,
what more can she want?

747
01:10:29,360 --> 01:10:31,359
They removed all tracks...

748
01:10:31,880 --> 01:10:33,719
That means Alcicek is alive.

749
01:10:35,480 --> 01:10:37,279
You're right but...

750
01:10:38,080 --> 01:10:39,919
...Ismihan doesn't want us to find her.

751
01:10:39,920 --> 01:10:41,919
She's up to something.

752
01:10:50,360 --> 01:10:51,559
Don't worry.

753
01:10:52,360 --> 01:10:54,319
I will tell you if something comes up.

754
01:10:55,400 --> 01:10:57,119
But I have no hope.

755
01:10:59,800 --> 01:11:01,719
Do not lose hope, Bengi

756
01:11:02,120 --> 01:11:04,879
We'll find our daughter safe and sound
with Allah's help.

757
01:11:06,640 --> 01:11:07,719
She has to be alive.

758
01:11:09,920 --> 01:11:10,759
I know it.

759
01:11:13,120 --> 01:11:14,149
I'll find them.

760
01:11:15,280 --> 01:11:17,359
We'll take the groom and our nephew back.

761
01:11:17,680 --> 01:11:19,799
We won’t leave them there.
Don't worry.

762
01:11:22,520 --> 01:11:24,439
Everyone knows what to do.

763
01:11:24,560 --> 01:11:27,399
I hope(if Allah permits)
we'll end this before sunrise.

764
01:11:48,280 --> 01:11:49,439
Hang on.

765
01:11:50,160 --> 01:11:51,719
Your father will save us.

766
01:12:06,800 --> 01:12:08,159
Aktemur.

767
01:12:09,800 --> 01:12:10,839
Where are you?

768
01:12:26,080 --> 01:12:27,239
Aktemur.

769
01:12:27,840 --> 01:12:29,079
Calm down first.

770
01:12:29,080 --> 01:12:30,759
How can I, mother?

771
01:12:30,920 --> 01:12:32,919
If they hurt her...

772
01:12:32,920 --> 01:12:34,679
They can't harm her.

773
01:12:34,680 --> 01:12:37,799
They can't harm your child or Alcicek.

774
01:12:37,800 --> 01:12:39,799
They’ll be just fine.

775
01:12:43,520 --> 01:12:45,679
I'll break the hands that try to reach her!

776
01:12:52,640 --> 01:12:53,439
She..

777
01:12:55,240 --> 01:12:56,399
They...

778
01:12:59,000 --> 01:13:00,519
...must be protected.

779
01:13:03,800 --> 01:13:04,919
Son...

780
01:13:08,200 --> 01:13:10,799
You entrusted them with Allah, son...

781
01:13:11,960 --> 01:13:13,919
If Allah permits...

782
01:13:13,920 --> 01:13:18,999
...Alcicek and our baby
will be okay, I hope.

783
01:13:19,120 --> 01:13:20,999
Have patience.

784
01:13:22,120 --> 01:13:23,199
Patience!!

785
01:13:24,920 --> 01:13:26,559
I couldn't protect them mother.

786
01:13:26,960 --> 01:13:29,559
I couldn't protect my tribe, my Hatun...

787
01:13:29,560 --> 01:13:32,159
I couldn't even protect my unborn baby!

788
01:13:32,200 --> 01:13:33,399
Aktemur...

789
01:13:33,880 --> 01:13:35,399
Stop.

790
01:13:54,800 --> 01:13:55,839
I will save you.

791
01:13:59,200 --> 01:14:01,239
I'll burn the whole world..

792
01:14:04,160 --> 01:14:05,559
..if I have to.

793
01:14:08,520 --> 01:14:09,719
Wait for me Alcicek.

794
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:11,879
Wait.

795
01:14:13,640 --> 01:14:16,479
Bursa Palace.

796
01:14:19,040 --> 01:14:21,479
You've met him, you know him more or less.

797
01:14:21,920 --> 01:14:23,399
How does he fight?

798
01:14:23,520 --> 01:14:26,439
Who does he trust?
Or, does he trust anyone?

799
01:14:26,440 --> 01:14:28,559
He trusts only his closest men.

800
01:14:28,640 --> 01:14:31,079
What's his weakness?

801
01:14:31,280 --> 01:14:33,759
Is his family more important...

802
01:14:34,200 --> 01:14:35,759
or his people?

803
01:14:36,040 --> 01:14:37,910
They are all the same for him, sir.

804
01:14:37,910 --> 01:14:41,799
I have been kept captive there.
The merchant is right. That’s why he’s so strong.

805
01:14:42,080 --> 01:14:43,039
And..

806
01:14:44,600 --> 01:14:45,839
...justice, sir.

807
01:14:50,120 --> 01:14:50,879
Justice?

808
01:14:54,880 --> 01:14:57,399
He waited at my door for hours.

809
01:14:58,760 --> 01:15:00,199
He didn’t get mad.

810
01:15:00,240 --> 01:15:01,479
He didn't leave.

811
01:15:01,840 --> 01:15:04,759
He just did what he had to.

812
01:15:05,680 --> 01:15:08,039
He didn’t react to any provocation of me.

813
01:15:08,040 --> 01:15:14,159
What is a shepherd who can do nothing
but serve in my kitchen...

814
01:15:14,680 --> 01:15:17,519
...doing here in front of me?

815
01:15:18,560 --> 01:15:19,999
He was patient.

816
01:15:20,800 --> 01:15:24,119
He just said what he had.

817
01:15:28,000 --> 01:15:30,079
And most importantly...

818
01:15:30,560 --> 01:15:33,959
...he saw things we thought he didn't.

819
01:15:38,720 --> 01:15:40,559
The archers.

820
01:15:43,960 --> 01:15:45,599
But..

821
01:15:49,200 --> 01:15:51,039
What if he realises again?

822
01:15:51,520 --> 01:15:53,039
Who?

823
01:15:56,120 --> 01:16:00,199
Who realises what, Lord Valens?

824
01:16:04,360 --> 01:16:07,879
I'm going to gauge out those eyes
he sees with today, Nayman.

825
01:16:10,720 --> 01:16:12,439
Let's leave.

826
01:16:19,720 --> 01:16:23,119
I told you that we would behead them.

827
01:16:23,440 --> 01:16:25,679
It's time now.

828
01:16:25,680 --> 01:16:27,679
Who will we kill my Bey?

829
01:16:28,560 --> 01:16:31,119
Lord Valens.

830
01:16:33,560 --> 01:16:35,239
He's gathering people.

831
01:16:35,240 --> 01:16:38,559
Even armies will come to support him
from west.

832
01:16:39,280 --> 01:16:41,279
But the real power..

833
01:16:41,280 --> 01:16:43,639
The real power is knowledge.

834
01:16:44,320 --> 01:16:50,719
We know where they are and
the secrets of those who are hidden.

835
01:16:51,360 --> 01:16:53,279
Are we going to kidnap them, my Bey?

836
01:16:53,280 --> 01:16:55,679
We will take down the leader.

837
01:16:58,560 --> 01:16:59,919
Now...

838
01:17:00,600 --> 01:17:02,639
...they're forming a big army.

839
01:17:03,440 --> 01:17:07,079
Even a huge army from the west is
coming to support them.

840
01:17:07,120 --> 01:17:11,959
We will take down the ones whom he trusts the most,
and his commanders.

841
01:17:13,640 --> 01:17:15,239
Cerkutay...

842
01:17:15,240 --> 01:17:17,879
...Konur, Baysungur and Gurbuz.

843
01:17:17,880 --> 01:17:19,879
You..

844
01:17:21,440 --> 01:17:24,639
..will go to Kestel

845
01:17:26,280 --> 01:17:27,639
Bayindir...

846
01:17:28,920 --> 01:17:32,519
...Huseyin, Turhan and Aykut,
you will go to Lefke.

847
01:17:32,520 --> 01:17:35,279
Everything is written in these.

848
01:17:35,880 --> 01:17:38,599
These are all for precaution.

849
01:17:38,800 --> 01:17:42,159
Who will go to take down the commanders
in the headquarters?

850
01:17:43,160 --> 01:17:44,799
I will confront them.

851
01:17:44,800 --> 01:17:46,799
Will you go alone, my Bey?

852
01:17:46,800 --> 01:17:49,079
I mean,
will you take them down by yourself?

853
01:17:51,400 --> 01:17:54,279
Foals grow up, horses get to rest...

854
01:17:54,920 --> 01:17:58,439
...the son grows up, the Bey gets to rest.

855
01:18:00,720 --> 01:18:02,839
Why are my sons here?

856
01:18:02,840 --> 01:18:05,719
They practiced so much.

857
01:18:05,720 --> 01:18:08,639
It's time to test them now.

858
01:18:12,320 --> 01:18:14,359
What are you waiting for alps?

859
01:18:14,360 --> 01:18:17,159
They will be tested against
the toughest opponents now...

860
01:18:17,160 --> 01:18:20,239
...so that they can withstand even tougher ones.

861
01:18:25,360 --> 01:18:26,479
My Bey.

862
01:18:26,480 --> 01:18:29,679
What we need is this kind of experience.

863
01:18:29,680 --> 01:18:32,919
Let us go through this and prove ourselves.
Is it easy to be a son of a Bey?

864
01:18:32,920 --> 01:18:34,359
There's my boy.

865
01:18:34,360 --> 01:18:35,999
Come on then.

866
01:18:36,280 --> 01:18:38,439
Everyone back to their duty!

867
01:18:56,480 --> 01:18:58,399
You shouldn't have come Aybars.

868
01:18:58,400 --> 01:19:00,639
I told you to stay at the tribe.

869
01:19:01,080 --> 01:19:03,639
I won't leave you alone aunt.

870
01:19:30,240 --> 01:19:32,759
Put down your swords.

871
01:20:01,040 --> 01:20:03,919
Are you afraid of two people?

872
01:20:04,560 --> 01:20:08,119
Right, you're not brave enough to face us.

873
01:20:08,480 --> 01:20:13,359
You sound too brave for a woman
whose daughter is missing, Bengi Hatun.

874
01:20:13,720 --> 01:20:15,599
You're a coward, Ismihan

875
01:20:15,720 --> 01:20:17,759
Enough to collaborate with your enemy...

876
01:20:17,880 --> 01:20:21,479
...and take innocent lives
for your own benefit!

877
01:20:21,560 --> 01:20:25,079
Enough!
You're not here to talk.

878
01:20:26,080 --> 01:20:29,559
You're here to be punished.

879
01:20:32,120 --> 01:20:35,079
Where's Alcicek?

880
01:20:58,360 --> 01:20:59,999
My girl...

881
01:21:00,240 --> 01:21:02,519
Alcicek!

882
01:21:08,240 --> 01:21:10,639
Let Alcicek go, Ismihan.

883
01:21:11,240 --> 01:21:14,079
You called me, here I am.

884
01:21:14,400 --> 01:21:16,519
Let Alcicek go and kill me.

885
01:21:16,760 --> 01:21:20,679
No.
It's not that easy.

886
01:21:21,280 --> 01:21:23,879
Not that easy, Bengi Hatun.

887
01:21:24,080 --> 01:21:26,719
You betrayed me!

888
01:21:27,200 --> 01:21:32,279
You messed everything up!

889
01:21:32,680 --> 01:21:36,439
My son lost the throne because of you!

890
01:21:37,280 --> 01:21:41,199
I will take both of your lives, Bengi Hatun!

891
01:21:41,560 --> 01:21:46,319
But first, I'll let you experience
the greatest pain in the world!

892
01:21:46,720 --> 01:21:48,879
Kill her!

893
01:21:48,960 --> 01:21:51,759
Alcicek!

894
01:22:26,200 --> 01:22:28,519
Oh, Haqq!

895
01:22:40,120 --> 01:22:42,029
In the name of Allah!

896
01:22:48,720 --> 01:22:50,999
It's over, Ismihan!

897
01:22:51,320 --> 01:22:54,439
Run, Alaeddin!
Run!

898
01:23:05,640 --> 01:23:07,759
Like you said, Osman Bey...

899
01:23:08,240 --> 01:23:10,799
Ismihan sent me a message.

900
01:23:11,160 --> 01:23:15,719
She wants me in return for Alcicek's life.

901
01:23:20,920 --> 01:23:22,519
It's a trap.

902
01:23:23,000 --> 01:23:25,319
She won't spare you or Alcicek.

903
01:23:25,920 --> 01:23:30,759
Once you're aware of the trap,
it becomes useless.

904
01:23:31,600 --> 01:23:33,879
You'll go there, Bengi Hatu

905
01:23:35,160 --> 01:23:37,279
What if they hurt Alcicek?

906
01:23:37,600 --> 01:23:41,239
Ismihan is capable of anything.
We'll be careful.

907
01:23:42,800 --> 01:23:44,119
MaIhun.

908
01:23:44,440 --> 01:23:45,759
Bala.

909
01:23:46,680 --> 01:23:47,959
Aktemur.

910
01:23:48,560 --> 01:23:50,799
Make your preparations.

911
01:23:51,160 --> 01:23:53,879
Be there before sunrise.

912
01:23:55,480 --> 01:23:58,399
As you command.

913
01:23:59,920 --> 01:24:01,199
Alaeddin is from us.

914
01:24:01,320 --> 01:24:02,939
Let's go after him!

915
01:24:21,520 --> 01:24:24,279
That's not Alcicek.

916
01:24:28,680 --> 01:24:31,199
Alcicek?

917
01:24:39,040 --> 01:24:44,839
You will never see your daughter again, Bengi.

918
01:24:49,760 --> 01:24:52,359
Where is Alcicek?

919
01:24:53,800 --> 01:24:56,879
She’s dead.

920
01:25:57,760 --> 01:26:00,399
Speak!
Where is Alcicek’?

921
01:26:01,960 --> 01:26:04,919
Alcicek is dead.

922
01:26:05,800 --> 01:26:08,159
I took your daughter from you, Bengi.

923
01:26:16,080 --> 01:26:17,439
Murderer!

924
01:26:17,440 --> 01:26:18,639
Traitor!

925
01:26:22,400 --> 01:26:24,199
Let go of me!

926
01:26:24,200 --> 01:26:27,839
My daughter was pregnant!
Alcicek was pregnant! Let go of me!

927
01:26:28,000 --> 01:26:30,359
She killed a young girl!

928
01:26:30,760 --> 01:26:33,999
Bengi!

929
01:26:37,560 --> 01:26:39,119
You did not kill her Ismihan.

930
01:26:40,120 --> 01:26:42,949
If you wanted to kill her,
you would have done it in front of Bengi.

931
01:26:42,949 --> 01:26:45,399
Now speak, where is Alcicek_

932
01:26:45,400 --> 01:26:47,999
You know me very well.

933
01:26:50,040 --> 01:26:55,199
I wanted to kill her in front of her mother.

934
01:26:57,800 --> 01:27:01,999
But while my men were trying to capture her...

935
01:27:02,760 --> 01:27:04,159
...they killed her.

936
01:27:07,720 --> 01:27:11,159
So I killed two of you, huh?

937
01:27:13,800 --> 01:27:15,559
But it's not enough.

938
01:27:15,560 --> 01:27:17,359
I will kill you too, Bengi.

939
01:27:17,920 --> 01:27:19,719
Ismihan!

940
01:27:23,160 --> 01:27:24,079
Let go!

941
01:27:24,080 --> 01:27:25,119
Bengi!

942
01:27:26,640 --> 01:27:31,239
You damn devil!
Speak, which of your men did this!?

943
01:27:41,200 --> 01:27:43,319
Where is Alcicek?

944
01:27:45,800 --> 01:27:48,159
Where is Alcicek?

945
01:27:48,480 --> 01:27:50,799
Get up! Speak!

946
01:27:51,080 --> 01:27:51,959
Dead.

947
01:27:52,080 --> 01:27:53,479
She is not dead!

948
01:27:54,160 --> 01:27:55,719
But I will hear it from you!

949
01:27:55,840 --> 01:27:58,079
Where is Alcicek?

950
01:27:58,240 --> 01:27:59,919
Stop.
Don't.

951
01:28:01,800 --> 01:28:03,199
I just followed the orders.

952
01:28:03,600 --> 01:28:05,439
I did what Mother Sultan asked me.

953
01:28:23,160 --> 01:28:24,279
Where is Alcicek?

954
01:28:28,600 --> 01:28:30,239
We ambushed them.

955
01:28:31,720 --> 01:28:32,719
She got away.

956
01:28:32,840 --> 01:28:35,079
She's in the forest up ahead.

957
01:28:36,600 --> 01:28:37,439
She's wounded.

958
01:28:52,440 --> 01:28:54,079
I'll deal with her.

959
01:28:54,640 --> 01:28:56,359
Find Alcicek. Go.

960
01:29:15,560 --> 01:29:18,159
I'll make you pay for this when the time comes.

961
01:29:18,560 --> 01:29:20,759
If Alcicek is hurt..

962
01:29:20,760 --> 01:29:22,919
...then you'll pay for it.

963
01:29:23,520 --> 01:29:25,199
Now shut up.

964
01:29:25,200 --> 01:29:27,159
Or I'll cut off your tongue.

965
01:29:28,040 --> 01:29:29,199
Mother.

966
01:29:29,280 --> 01:29:30,159
Alaeddin.

967
01:29:30,680 --> 01:29:32,239
Malhun Hatun.

968
01:29:34,440 --> 01:29:36,479
Give Ismihan to us.

969
01:29:36,960 --> 01:29:40,039
Only after Alcicek is found.

970
01:29:40,640 --> 01:29:42,799
If Alcicek is hurt...

971
01:29:44,240 --> 01:29:46,719
,,..no one can take this devil from us.

972
01:29:48,080 --> 01:29:49,199
Alps!

973
01:29:49,240 --> 01:29:51,199
We'll go back to Yenisehir.

974
01:29:59,360 --> 01:30:00,559
Sons.

975
01:30:00,640 --> 01:30:02,559
This is harder than a battle.

976
01:30:04,000 --> 01:30:05,399
Sometimes, we need to be quiet.

977
01:30:05,720 --> 01:30:07,839
We need to hide.

978
01:30:08,040 --> 01:30:10,159
And we need to wear disguises.

979
01:30:10,160 --> 01:30:11,599
But most importantly...

980
01:30:12,720 --> 01:30:14,479
...we need to hide our daggers.

981
01:30:16,440 --> 01:30:17,119
Orhan.

982
01:30:17,520 --> 01:30:19,479
How many daggers do I have on me?

983
01:30:57,520 --> 01:30:58,999
These two.

984
01:31:01,400 --> 01:31:03,759
Alaeddin. Go ahead, son.

985
01:31:27,720 --> 01:31:30,599
There was one more, huh?

986
01:31:33,720 --> 01:31:35,199
Sons.

987
01:31:35,200 --> 01:31:39,079
If the guards
where you're going are like you...

988
01:31:39,080 --> 01:31:41,719
...how tough it is for those commanders!

989
01:31:49,000 --> 01:31:50,599
Firstly...

990
01:31:51,080 --> 01:31:54,079
...you check everywhere closely.

991
01:31:57,480 --> 01:31:59,599
That's one.

992
01:32:04,680 --> 01:32:07,319
And that's two.

993
01:32:14,120 --> 01:32:16,279
And that's three.

994
01:32:19,480 --> 01:32:21,199
What's important...

995
01:32:21,200 --> 01:32:26,039
..is that you hide your swords and
daggers in the best way possible.

996
01:32:27,960 --> 01:32:29,879
Right sons?

997
01:32:47,000 --> 01:32:48,719
Sons.

998
01:32:48,720 --> 01:32:51,319
The most important thing
is to be quite.

999
01:32:52,280 --> 01:32:56,239
Even if you step on a branch,
that noise can be the end of you.

1000
01:32:56,240 --> 01:32:58,799
That's why you’ll be careful.
Okay?

1001
01:32:59,320 --> 01:33:00,799
Let's go now.

1002
01:34:09,760 --> 01:34:11,279
My sons.

1003
01:34:11,440 --> 01:34:14,799
So you separated into two wings...

1004
01:34:15,800 --> 01:34:18,999
...and surprised him from both sides...

1005
01:34:20,280 --> 01:34:24,399
...when he least expected it.

1006
01:34:25,560 --> 01:34:26,639
Good.

1007
01:34:27,000 --> 01:34:28,199
Good.

1008
01:34:28,360 --> 01:34:31,479
We did think
we could surprise him, my Bey.

1009
01:34:32,600 --> 01:34:34,239
Well done.

1010
01:34:34,600 --> 01:34:38,519
If one of us falls down,
the other can drive the dagger, my Bey.

1011
01:34:39,720 --> 01:34:42,919
Oi praise be! My Beys.

1012
01:34:43,520 --> 01:34:47,199
They’re clearly going to play
with the infidels, my Bey.

1013
01:34:47,320 --> 01:34:48,439
Of course.

1014
01:34:48,600 --> 01:34:52,959
They’ve been going through
their training for a reason.

1015
01:34:55,200 --> 01:34:59,839
Now the next one.

1016
01:35:17,440 --> 01:35:19,559
Come, Orhan.

1017
01:35:41,400 --> 01:35:43,279
Alaeddin.

1018
01:36:02,240 --> 01:36:06,559
My sons, I know you are skilled archers.

1019
01:36:07,200 --> 01:36:09,439
But that is different.

1020
01:36:10,000 --> 01:36:13,359
You will hit the small target away.

1021
01:36:14,000 --> 01:36:17,679
It may look easy, but it is not.

1022
01:36:19,840 --> 01:36:22,319
This is a sharp shoot. Now.

1023
01:36:24,440 --> 01:36:25,919
Orhan, move.

1024
01:36:32,560 --> 01:36:34,279
Closer.

1025
01:36:36,880 --> 01:36:40,559
Now, look at your target
and find yourself a gap.

1026
01:36:40,600 --> 01:36:41,999
Exactly.

1027
01:36:45,640 --> 01:36:47,119
Focus.

1028
01:36:47,920 --> 01:36:49,199
Breathe.

1029
01:36:50,520 --> 01:36:52,079
Now...

1030
01:36:52,480 --> 01:36:55,039
...you will look 5 span above your target.

1031
01:36:59,520 --> 01:37:01,639
When you are sure...

1032
01:37:03,040 --> 01:37:04,679
...hold your breath.

1033
01:37:09,080 --> 01:37:10,479
Shoot.

1034
01:37:20,760 --> 01:37:21,959
Alaeddin.

1035
01:37:22,599 --> 01:37:23,599
Your turn.

1036
01:37:27,960 --> 01:37:30,439
Closer. Closer.

1037
01:37:35,520 --> 01:37:36,919
Look at your target.

1038
01:37:37,800 --> 01:37:39,759
Look look look look.

1039
01:37:40,160 --> 01:37:42,999
Breathe in, move your elbow.

1040
01:37:47,040 --> 01:37:48,399
Now..

1041
01:37:49,400 --> 01:37:51,039
...hold your breath...

1042
01:37:52,680 --> 01:37:54,039
...and shoot.

1043
01:38:00,800 --> 01:38:02,119
Come here.

1044
01:38:04,560 --> 01:38:08,399
Praise be!
My sons, just as I said...

1045
01:38:09,000 --> 01:38:10,799
...you hit the target in the eye.

1046
01:38:15,680 --> 01:38:18,919
My Bey, we got word from alps,
they arrived.

1047
01:38:19,400 --> 01:38:21,439
Then we should strike at the same time.

1048
01:38:21,440 --> 01:38:22,719
Let's go quickly.

1049
01:38:24,400 --> 01:38:25,839
Come on my sons.

1050
01:38:31,920 --> 01:38:34,599
Kestel Church.

1051
01:38:55,440 --> 01:38:56,919
What's wrong my son?

1052
01:39:05,560 --> 01:39:07,199
I sinned, father.

1053
01:39:07,360 --> 01:39:09,799
Speak, my child,
that's why I am here.

1054
01:39:10,120 --> 01:39:12,599
But I have never seen you
at the church before.

1055
01:39:17,600 --> 01:39:19,679
I go from church to church...

1056
01:39:22,040 --> 01:39:23,919
...and search for a remedy for my soul.

1057
01:39:24,040 --> 01:39:25,999
But I can’t find it.

1058
01:39:28,320 --> 01:39:30,759
What blackens your soul like this?

1059
01:39:42,080 --> 01:39:43,959
I killed many men.

1060
01:39:44,720 --> 01:39:46,319
Christians.

1061
01:39:47,880 --> 01:39:49,879
God is forgiving.

1062
01:39:50,240 --> 01:39:52,399
If you did not enjoy....

1063
01:39:52,400 --> 01:39:55,839
...and if you regret it,
God will forgive you.

1064
01:40:03,760 --> 01:40:09,079
I enjoy cutting infidels, father.

1065
01:40:12,560 --> 01:40:17,159
Churches have always been graves for you!
Lord Valens said that you would come!

1066
01:40:17,640 --> 01:40:18,879
Attack!

1067
01:40:23,880 --> 01:40:27,519
You all want to kill me,
but none of you can!

1068
01:40:28,160 --> 01:40:29,679
Oh Allah!

1069
01:40:39,680 --> 01:40:40,559
They are coming!

1070
01:40:40,560 --> 01:40:42,479
I will come back.

1071
01:40:42,560 --> 01:40:44,239
They are running way!
Capture them!

1072
01:40:50,600 --> 01:40:51,959
Akte...

1073
01:40:52,280 --> 01:40:53,599
Aktemur..

1074
01:40:55,960 --> 01:40:57,359
Aktemur..

1075
01:41:00,200 --> 01:41:03,399
Alps!
You will search the trunk of every tree!

1076
01:41:05,640 --> 01:41:06,719
No.

1077
01:41:06,880 --> 01:41:09,559
We'll find her.

1078
01:41:09,560 --> 01:41:11,559
No matter what, we'll find her!

1079
01:41:11,640 --> 01:41:14,159
Allah help us, my Creator.

1080
01:41:14,160 --> 01:41:17,119
Alcicek!

1081
01:41:17,360 --> 01:41:18,119
She’s alive.

1082
01:41:18,560 --> 01:41:21,559
She's alive. Mothers can feel it.

1083
01:41:21,560 --> 01:41:23,079
My girl's breathing.

1084
01:41:23,760 --> 01:41:25,159
Keep praying to Allah.

1085
01:41:26,000 --> 01:41:26,799
We'll find her.

1086
01:41:27,640 --> 01:41:28,399
We'll find her.

1087
01:41:29,560 --> 01:41:30,799
Alcicek!

1088
01:41:30,800 --> 01:41:32,959
- Daughter, speak!
- Alcicek!

1089
01:41:39,820 --> 01:41:42,839
A rich and smart merchant..

1090
01:41:42,880 --> 01:41:46,079
...can find the best goods to buy.

1091
01:41:46,840 --> 01:41:48,079
But...

1092
01:41:49,480 --> 01:41:51,799
..there is one thing..

1093
01:41:53,360 --> 01:41:55,799
...you can't buy with money.

1094
01:41:56,200 --> 01:41:57,319
Yes.

1095
01:41:57,320 --> 01:42:02,719
And that is Yagiz slave.

1096
01:42:04,800 --> 01:42:07,559
I understand,
but a Turk can't be a slave.

1097
01:42:07,560 --> 01:42:10,479
Astagfirullah. Of course.

1098
01:42:10,480 --> 01:42:13,159
But we have to. That's the game.

1099
01:42:13,520 --> 01:42:17,599
Listen. You'll be a slave first.

1100
01:42:18,080 --> 01:42:21,359
Then we'll cut heads.

1101
01:42:23,520 --> 01:42:24,659
Bayindir Bey.

1102
01:42:25,680 --> 01:42:27,199
Why am the thief?

1103
01:42:27,200 --> 01:42:28,359
Why not something else?

1104
01:42:28,400 --> 01:42:31,559
This is just a game.

1105
01:42:32,360 --> 01:42:35,519
Just steal my pouch at the market.

1106
01:42:36,800 --> 01:42:39,839
He will run and catch you.

1107
01:42:40,120 --> 01:42:45,919
Then all the people will see
how strong and fast he is.

1108
01:42:47,480 --> 01:42:52,479
And then two merchants
will come to buy him from me.

1109
01:42:52,520 --> 01:42:57,079
And after that the biggest battle will begin.

1110
01:42:57,080 --> 01:43:00,839
Osman Bey gave me this duty.

1111
01:43:02,880 --> 01:43:04,679
Come on. Let's get back to duty.

1112
01:43:06,240 --> 01:43:08,919
Come on. In the name of Allah.

1113
01:43:31,760 --> 01:43:34,399
A rich merchant...

1114
01:43:34,560 --> 01:43:37,759
...gets the best goods.

1115
01:43:46,280 --> 01:43:47,959
Over there. Stop

1116
01:43:48,080 --> 01:43:49,239
I said stop!

1117
01:43:51,200 --> 01:43:52,799
There are so many thieves.

1118
01:43:53,000 --> 01:43:54,799
Our dear Lord in heaven.

1119
01:43:54,880 --> 01:43:59,679
Ever since you sank my ships
in the Red Sea...

1120
01:43:59,840 --> 01:44:03,679
...you've never answered my prayers.

1121
01:44:08,840 --> 01:44:12,959
My slave deserves every inch of
the gold I'll give him.

1122
01:44:13,400 --> 01:44:14,959
May God bless you.

1123
01:44:15,400 --> 01:44:16,119
Wait.

1124
01:44:18,320 --> 01:44:21,159
Don't.
The fear is a good punishment.

1125
01:44:21,880 --> 01:44:22,799
Let him be.

1126
01:44:29,720 --> 01:44:31,639
May God bless you.

1127
01:44:32,320 --> 01:44:34,599
My dear friend!

1128
01:44:34,600 --> 01:44:38,399
You are no slave, you’re a dear friend!

1129
01:44:40,960 --> 01:44:44,279
If I didn't have to, I'd never sell you!

1130
01:44:47,240 --> 01:44:49,919
But it's life.

1131
01:44:51,120 --> 01:44:52,439
Walk.

1132
01:45:01,240 --> 01:45:03,319
No one's coming Bayindir Bey.

1133
01:45:04,120 --> 01:45:06,719
They will. They will.

1134
01:45:08,880 --> 01:45:12,639
Merchants always follow a fallen seller.

1135
01:45:12,640 --> 01:45:14,599
They will come eventually.

1136
01:45:15,560 --> 01:45:19,999
We praised our slave and presented well.

1137
01:45:22,840 --> 01:45:24,999
They will come eventually.

1138
01:45:30,000 --> 01:45:31,119
It's a trap!

1139
01:45:36,760 --> 01:45:38,319
Now it's time...

1140
01:45:38,920 --> 01:45:41,199
...to shed some blood.

1141
01:46:23,560 --> 01:46:24,929
Run!

1142
01:46:56,600 --> 01:46:58,319
Father.

1143
01:47:00,240 --> 01:47:02,599
Is it you?

1144
01:47:14,160 --> 01:47:15,279
Mother.

1145
01:47:15,280 --> 01:47:17,199
This won't do.

1146
01:47:17,200 --> 01:47:19,239
The sun is about to set.

1147
01:47:19,240 --> 01:47:20,479
You’re right.

1148
01:47:20,480 --> 01:47:22,039
Alcicek.

1149
01:47:22,040 --> 01:47:23,319
If something happens to her...

1150
01:47:23,320 --> 01:47:26,599
It's not the time Bengi,
we can't lose hope.

1151
01:47:26,600 --> 01:47:29,359
We will find both of them safe.

1152
01:47:29,360 --> 01:47:31,959
We'll play with our grandkid, hold on.

1153
01:47:31,960 --> 01:47:33,039
If Allah permits...

1154
01:47:33,040 --> 01:47:35,319
If Allah permits, Ayse, if Allah permits.

1155
01:47:38,800 --> 01:47:40,839
Alcicek!

1156
01:47:40,840 --> 01:47:41,839
Let's separate!

1157
01:47:41,840 --> 01:47:43,919
You go that way and
we’ll go this way.

1158
01:47:43,920 --> 01:47:45,319
Come on alps!

1159
01:47:45,320 --> 01:47:47,479
Split up!

1160
01:47:52,280 --> 01:47:54,879
Forgive me, my child.

1161
01:47:55,360 --> 01:47:57,239
I failed to protect you.

1162
01:48:03,240 --> 01:48:05,119
Alcicek.

1163
01:48:05,720 --> 01:48:08,079
Alcicek.

1164
01:48:12,040 --> 01:48:14,399
I'm going to find you
no matter what it takes.

1165
01:48:15,840 --> 01:48:16,959
My Allah...

1166
01:48:18,120 --> 01:48:19,999
My Allah show me the way.

1167
01:48:22,360 --> 01:48:24,359
Alcicek!

1168
01:48:25,960 --> 01:48:27,159
Alcicek!

1169
01:48:29,400 --> 01:48:31,199
Aktemur!

1170
01:48:34,920 --> 01:48:36,999
Alcicek!

1171
01:48:38,640 --> 01:48:40,599
-Alcicek.
-Aktemur.

1172
01:48:42,080 --> 01:48:43,599
Alcicek?

1173
01:48:46,240 --> 01:48:47,639
Alcicek.

1174
01:48:48,400 --> 01:48:49,919
Alcicek.

1175
01:48:52,840 --> 01:48:55,079
Alcicek.

1176
01:48:55,920 --> 01:48:57,159
Alcicek.

1177
01:48:57,160 --> 01:49:00,439
You're okay.

1178
01:49:00,960 --> 01:49:02,239
Are you okay?

1179
01:49:02,240 --> 01:49:03,879
Aktemur.

1180
01:49:03,880 --> 01:49:05,679
My baby.

1181
01:49:05,840 --> 01:49:06,959
Baby...

1182
01:49:10,080 --> 01:49:14,599
Kumral Abdal!
Kumral Abdal!!!

1183
01:49:17,280 --> 01:49:18,119
You're okay.

1184
01:49:18,120 --> 01:49:20,359
Okay.
Our baby is okay too.

1185
01:49:20,360 --> 01:49:22,879
Mother!

1186
01:49:23,960 --> 01:49:25,279
Kumral Abdal, come.

1187
01:49:26,320 --> 01:49:28,279
Mother Bengi!

1188
01:49:29,400 --> 01:49:30,719
Aktemur!

1189
01:49:31,400 --> 01:49:33,279
Alcicek!

1190
01:49:33,280 --> 01:49:34,639
Tell me she's alive, son.

1191
01:49:34,640 --> 01:49:36,279
She's alive thank Allah.

1192
01:49:36,280 --> 01:49:39,559
She's alive. Thank Allah. Thank Allah.
Come on.

1193
01:49:39,960 --> 01:49:40,999
My baby.

1194
01:49:42,480 --> 01:49:43,959
Alcicek.

1195
01:49:44,760 --> 01:49:46,719
Is she okay?
Is she okay?

1196
01:49:46,720 --> 01:49:48,199
Aunt..

1197
01:49:48,200 --> 01:49:49,919
Alcicek!

1198
01:49:50,560 --> 01:49:51,559
Daughter.

1199
01:49:51,560 --> 01:49:53,599
Thank Allah. Thank Allah.

1200
01:49:57,720 --> 01:49:59,839
Thank Allah.

1201
01:49:59,840 --> 01:50:01,399
She's okay, she's okay.

1202
01:50:01,400 --> 01:50:03,799
But we need to go to Yenisehir quickly.

1203
01:50:03,800 --> 01:50:05,719
Come on.

1204
01:50:05,720 --> 01:50:08,759
- Come on.
-Alps bring the horses at once!

1205
01:50:09,960 --> 01:50:11,119
Get up.

1206
01:50:11,280 --> 01:50:13,119
Come on daughter.

1207
01:50:18,640 --> 01:50:21,359
Thank God the armies will arrive.

1208
01:50:21,640 --> 01:50:24,439
We will get rid of the Turks for good.

1209
01:50:24,880 --> 01:50:27,319
You should thank God, my friend Milos..

1210
01:50:27,600 --> 01:50:30,119
Once the armies are here..

1211
01:50:30,200 --> 01:50:32,319
I will be working with the devil.

1212
01:50:32,320 --> 01:50:33,479
Byzantine...

1213
01:50:33,480 --> 01:50:37,719
...owes you commanders a lot.
When you lead the armies...

1214
01:50:37,720 --> 01:50:40,839
..Turks will be banished from everywhere
Konya included.

1215
01:50:40,840 --> 01:50:44,759
Once the other armies join us...

1216
01:50:45,120 --> 01:50:48,599
...the Muslims will be done forever!

1217
01:51:30,560 --> 01:51:32,319
Are you looking for us?

1218
01:51:55,960 --> 01:51:57,879
Good job, boys.

1219
01:51:58,000 --> 01:51:59,599
Good job.

1220
01:52:00,200 --> 01:52:02,439
They're skilled, my Bey.

1221
01:52:03,000 --> 01:52:04,079
Of course they are.

1222
01:52:04,440 --> 01:52:07,319
It's going to be much worse over there,
my sons.

1223
01:52:08,000 --> 01:52:12,999
Even the slightest sound
might cause us our lives.

1224
01:52:15,240 --> 01:52:17,199
So be quiet.

1225
01:52:39,200 --> 01:52:41,879
The armies will be here.

1226
01:52:42,200 --> 01:52:44,199
I'll march on Yenisehir and Sogut.

1227
01:52:44,680 --> 01:52:47,439
You will take Inegol and
Bilecik with your armies.

1228
01:52:48,320 --> 01:52:49,919
-Commander Mateus.
-Yes, sir?

1229
01:52:50,040 --> 01:52:54,519
You will set
the remaining tribes on fire!

1230
01:52:55,520 --> 01:52:58,119
After all, you have experience
regarding the matter.

1231
01:52:59,680 --> 01:53:02,749
You're much more experienced
when it comes to killing Turks.

1232
01:53:03,040 --> 01:53:07,519
The armies will be victorious
under your command.

1233
01:53:42,640 --> 01:53:45,079
My sons.

1234
01:53:45,520 --> 01:53:48,759
...that's our target.

1235
01:53:51,880 --> 01:53:54,599
Take a good look at him.

1236
01:53:55,120 --> 01:53:56,399
Orhan.

1237
01:53:56,720 --> 01:53:58,719
Alaeddin.

1238
01:53:59,280 --> 01:54:02,079
You will take down the one on the right.

1239
01:54:02,640 --> 01:54:06,559
You will shoot two arrows
and finish them both at once.

1240
01:54:07,400 --> 01:54:08,919
-Boran.
-My Bey.

1241
01:54:09,120 --> 01:54:11,159
Take the one on the left..

1242
01:54:11,880 --> 01:54:14,199
...and I'll take the one in the middle.

1243
01:54:15,040 --> 01:54:17,439
We'll attack them as one.

1244
01:54:17,960 --> 01:54:19,799
Let's go.

1245
01:54:20,280 --> 01:54:21,799
May Allah bless our War.

1246
01:54:21,800 --> 01:54:22,639
Ameen, my Bey.

1247
01:54:22,639 --> 01:54:23,639
Go now.

1248
01:54:54,320 --> 01:54:57,719
What are you doing here?

1249
01:54:58,160 --> 01:55:01,239
Osman.

1250
01:55:12,080 --> 01:55:15,999
You didn't expect to see me, did you?

1251
01:55:16,320 --> 01:55:19,159
I will kill you now.

1252
01:55:19,680 --> 01:55:21,039
It's over!

1253
01:55:21,440 --> 01:55:23,199
How did you find me?

1254
01:55:24,280 --> 01:55:26,839
I tried to think like you.

1255
01:55:28,080 --> 01:55:30,399
I taught myself how to think like you.

1256
01:55:30,600 --> 01:55:35,319
I told you not to mistake me for others.

1257
01:55:35,640 --> 01:55:37,479
I know about every step you take.

1258
01:55:38,080 --> 01:55:39,919
I know you, Osman.

1259
01:55:56,680 --> 01:55:58,759
Get out of here, sons.

1260
01:55:58,880 --> 01:56:01,199
We won't leave you, father.

1261
01:56:02,360 --> 01:56:03,879
Get out of here!

1262
01:56:04,640 --> 01:56:07,639
Come on.

1263
01:56:19,160 --> 01:56:21,079
Let's go

1264
01:56:21,680 --> 01:56:23,039
Oh, Haqq!

1265
01:56:23,680 --> 01:56:25,159
Go with them, Boran.

1266
01:56:25,240 --> 01:56:26,519
I won't leave you, my Bey.

1267
01:56:26,600 --> 01:56:28,279
-I won't you, my Bey.
- Boran!

1268
01:56:28,360 --> 01:56:30,519
-Boran!
-We can do it, my Bey.

1269
01:56:30,720 --> 01:56:33,239
Your sons will run,
we'll go after them.

1270
01:56:33,880 --> 01:56:36,559
We'll do it together, my Bey.

1271
01:56:37,800 --> 01:56:40,759
I'll cover you, my Bey.

1272
01:56:45,760 --> 01:56:47,039
Go!

1273
01:56:47,080 --> 01:56:47,879
Now!

1274
01:56:56,520 --> 01:56:58,079
My Bey!

1275
01:57:06,120 --> 01:57:07,319
My Bey, are you okay?

1276
01:57:07,320 --> 01:57:09,519
I am okay, this is nothing!

1277
01:57:09,880 --> 01:57:11,599
We went through worse!

1278
01:57:15,200 --> 01:57:18,599
You will see Valens!

1279
01:57:32,080 --> 01:57:33,679
Stop resisting, Osman!

1280
01:57:36,360 --> 01:57:39,439
Your beloved sons...

1281
01:57:39,760 --> 01:57:42,439
...will die in my hands!

1282
01:57:46,280 --> 01:57:49,199
And don't walk near the trees.

1283
01:57:49,760 --> 01:57:55,319
There are traps I prepared
for you in the forest!

1284
01:57:55,560 --> 01:57:59,479
Just because I did not spill your blood,
you act this way!

1285
01:58:00,160 --> 01:58:03,159
You can speak so highly because of that!

1286
01:58:04,320 --> 01:58:08,359
I am going to bury you
in the middle of Bursa’

1287
01:58:08,840 --> 01:58:11,159
Kill them!

1288
01:58:13,600 --> 01:58:15,279
I will come for you!

1289
01:58:15,280 --> 01:58:17,679
You will not be able to leave, Osman!

1290
01:58:18,400 --> 01:58:21,279
You will all die in this forest!

1291
01:58:21,400 --> 01:58:21,959
Boran!

1292
01:58:21,960 --> 01:58:22,919
Come on my Bey!

1293
01:58:42,280 --> 01:58:43,759
Where is the dungeon?

1294
01:58:44,480 --> 01:58:45,999
I can’t say.

1295
01:58:46,320 --> 01:58:49,639
If you have a request, tell me,
I will speak to Malhun Hatun.

1296
01:58:51,520 --> 01:58:54,559
Do you know who you are talking to?

1297
01:58:55,560 --> 01:58:58,959
I do not take anyone’s permission.

1298
01:58:59,920 --> 01:59:03,679
Tell me where the dungeon is.
I have questions for Ismihan.

1299
01:59:06,200 --> 01:59:08,279
He is doing his duty.

1300
01:59:10,720 --> 01:59:12,079
But...

1301
01:59:14,240 --> 01:59:16,599
...you don’t know where you stand, Hatun.

1302
01:59:19,080 --> 01:59:22,999
This is my mansion, watch your mouth here!

1303
01:59:23,680 --> 01:59:27,479
I am responsible for those in the dungeon,
Malhun Hatun.

1304
01:59:28,280 --> 01:59:31,599
And it's my duty to question them.

1305
01:59:31,840 --> 01:59:34,279
Now show me where the dungeon is.

1306
01:59:34,560 --> 01:59:37,079
I have things to talk with Ismihan.

1307
01:59:37,960 --> 01:59:40,119
Don't confuse me with anyone else, Hatun.

1308
01:59:40,560 --> 01:59:42,919
You have no power here.

1309
01:59:43,440 --> 01:59:46,279
You can't order me.

1310
01:59:48,560 --> 01:59:51,999
I will never allow you to
speak alone with Ismihan.

1311
01:59:54,960 --> 01:59:58,039
Gorkluce, bring the prisoners here.

1312
02:00:02,080 --> 02:00:03,359
Whatever you want to speak with her,
you will speak in front of me.

1313
02:00:04,960 --> 02:00:08,079
Don't you trust me, Malhun Hatun?

1314
02:00:10,560 --> 02:00:12,839
This is the borderlands, Hatun.

1315
02:00:13,600 --> 02:00:17,439
We learned that we shouldn't trust
anyone the hard way!

1316
02:00:24,520 --> 02:00:29,719
You brought this upon us due to your arrogance, mother.
You ruined us just to take revenge from Bengi!

1317
02:00:36,600 --> 02:00:39,439
Come on, get ready.

1318
02:00:41,200 --> 02:00:43,079
Where are we going?

1319
02:01:25,480 --> 02:01:28,599
I saved Osman Bey's life.

1320
02:01:28,600 --> 02:01:31,959
And you are still not trusting me,
Malhun Hatun?

1321
02:01:33,080 --> 02:01:36,279
I hope you are doing this
out of your responsibility to the state.

1322
02:01:37,320 --> 02:01:42,159
If it’s out of arrogance,
it is Ismihan who is the most arrogant one!

1323
02:01:42,920 --> 02:01:45,279
And her punishment is obvious!

1324
02:01:48,040 --> 02:01:50,159
We will take our precaution.

1325
02:01:51,160 --> 02:01:53,599
...you may think of us as arrogant.

1326
02:01:55,360 --> 02:01:57,719
There is no need to hurry, Hatun.

1327
02:01:58,040 --> 02:02:00,999
When we find Alcicek..

1328
02:02:01,280 --> 02:02:05,079
..we will give Ismihan
and Alaeddin to you.

1329
02:02:22,120 --> 02:02:24,439
Prepare the infirmary immediately!

1330
02:02:25,230 --> 02:02:27,789
Prepare the infirmary!
Call The Dark Midwife!

1331
02:02:33,880 --> 02:02:35,239
Aktemur, is she okay?

1332
02:02:35,240 --> 02:02:37,169
Thank Allah, aunt,
she will get better.

1333
02:02:37,169 --> 02:02:38,399
Come on, carry her.

1334
02:02:38,560 --> 02:02:41,639
Ulgen!
Bring hot water and clean towels!

1335
02:02:44,360 --> 02:02:46,399
Come on!

1336
02:02:46,960 --> 02:02:48,079
Beng,

1337
02:02:48,760 --> 02:02:50,799
-She's fine.
-She will get better.

1338
02:02:53,840 --> 02:02:55,439
Bengi Hatun!

1339
02:03:02,200 --> 02:03:03,639
Isn't she dead?

1340
02:03:08,520 --> 02:03:09,559
She's almost dead.

1341
02:03:10,720 --> 02:03:11,639
Good.

1342
02:03:13,320 --> 02:03:16,359
She'll die right in front of her mother.

1343
02:03:17,320 --> 02:03:18,919
What are you saying?

1344
02:03:20,480 --> 02:03:21,879
What are you saying?

1345
02:03:22,040 --> 02:03:24,359
It's over. I killed her.

1346
02:03:26,160 --> 02:03:27,119
Then..

1347
02:03:27,960 --> 02:03:30,959
I will kill you Bengi Hatun.

1348
02:03:30,960 --> 02:03:33,919
Ismihan.
Ismihan I'll kill you.

1349
02:03:33,920 --> 02:03:36,249
Ismihan!

1350
02:03:36,340 --> 02:03:38,239
Bengi!
Enough!

1351
02:03:40,960 --> 02:03:42,319
She'll live.

1352
02:03:43,800 --> 02:03:45,639
Because she has loved ones.

1353
02:03:46,080 --> 02:03:47,639
We pray for her.

1354
02:03:52,360 --> 02:03:54,079
She's not like you Ismihan.

1355
02:03:55,240 --> 02:03:56,399
But you..

1356
02:03:56,760 --> 02:03:58,919
...your fate is clear.

1357
02:03:59,200 --> 02:04:00,919
You'll rot in a dungeon.

1358
02:04:06,320 --> 02:04:07,879
Bengi.

1359
02:04:09,200 --> 02:04:11,679
Alcicek's inside.
Go to her.

1360
02:04:14,120 --> 02:04:15,079
Go on.

1361
02:04:26,840 --> 02:04:28,039
Esrigun Hatun.

1362
02:04:28,720 --> 02:04:30,399
You can have her now.

1363
02:04:33,480 --> 02:04:35,519
Prepare the carriages.

1364
02:04:35,800 --> 02:04:38,119
Come on Alps!
Take her.

1365
02:04:39,280 --> 02:04:40,879
This won't end here.

1366
02:04:41,360 --> 02:04:43,639
I will be back.

1367
02:04:43,960 --> 02:04:45,639
Wait for that day.

1368
02:04:52,400 --> 02:04:53,359
Aral.

1369
02:04:54,400 --> 02:04:55,639
Be cautious.

1370
02:04:55,680 --> 02:04:58,559
Make sure the caravan's protected.

1371
02:04:58,840 --> 02:05:01,959
They will go to Gazan Khan
in one piece.

1372
02:05:02,600 --> 02:05:05,279
Be careful. I don't want problems.

1373
02:05:12,000 --> 02:05:13,679
What is it Esrigun Hatun?

1374
02:05:15,680 --> 02:05:17,239
What do you mean "they"?

1375
02:05:17,840 --> 02:05:19,239
Won't you go with them?

1376
02:05:21,760 --> 02:05:22,439
No.

1377
02:05:23,480 --> 02:05:24,999
I won't Malhun Hatun.

1378
02:05:27,920 --> 02:05:30,759
I didn’t know what this place was like.

1379
02:05:31,440 --> 02:05:33,319
The borders are in chaos.

1380
02:05:35,080 --> 02:05:36,519
Fixing this...

1381
02:05:37,160 --> 02:05:38,519
...is my job.

1382
02:06:02,870 --> 02:06:03,839
My Bey!

1383
02:06:10,360 --> 02:06:11,239
My Bey.

1384
02:06:24,440 --> 02:06:26,519
Sons. Sons... Boran.

1385
02:06:26,640 --> 02:06:27,719
My sons.

1386
02:06:30,720 --> 02:06:31,439
My sons.

1387
02:06:31,440 --> 02:06:33,079
They're okay. They're running.

1388
02:06:33,080 --> 02:06:35,119
-Where are my sons?
-They're escaping.

1389
02:06:35,120 --> 02:06:37,119
They’re okay My Bey. Don't worry.

1390
02:06:37,880 --> 02:06:38,759
Are you okay my Bey?

1391
02:06:38,760 --> 02:06:40,759
I'm okay. I'm okay. I'm okay.

1392
02:06:40,960 --> 02:06:42,759
Valens. Valens.

1393
02:06:44,360 --> 02:06:45,839
Valens.

1394
02:06:47,880 --> 02:06:48,639
My sons.

1395
02:06:48,640 --> 02:06:50,639
We ran out of arrows.

1396
02:06:51,520 --> 02:06:53,799
We won't stop until we find my sons.

1397
02:06:54,720 --> 02:06:57,359
We won't my Bey.
We won't.

1398
02:06:59,680 --> 02:07:01,719
Don't let them get away.

1399
02:07:03,240 --> 02:07:05,679
I want Osman dead.

1400
02:07:05,680 --> 02:07:08,119
I want his sons dead.

1401
02:07:08,280 --> 02:07:10,119
You can't get away.

1402
02:07:21,080 --> 02:07:22,839
Come on.

1403
02:08:39,880 --> 02:08:41,199
They’re coming brother.

1404
02:08:41,200 --> 02:08:43,199
Hide Alaeddin. Hide.

1405
02:08:47,520 --> 02:08:50,399
Let them come. Let them come.

1406
02:08:56,400 --> 02:08:57,959
Alaeddin, on my mark.

1407
02:09:02,480 --> 02:09:03,839
Now.

1408
02:09:08,560 --> 02:09:09,799
Come on.

1409
02:09:17,160 --> 02:09:18,719
This way.

1410
02:09:28,880 --> 02:09:31,519
Alaeddin it's a trap don’t get up.

1411
02:09:34,920 --> 02:09:36,799
Come on. Come on.

1412
02:09:41,920 --> 02:09:43,439
I won't wait anymore.

1413
02:09:43,440 --> 02:09:44,079
I am going.

1414
02:09:44,080 --> 02:09:46,479
Hold on son, wait. Be a little patient.

1415
02:09:46,480 --> 02:09:49,119
I don’t have any left mother, I’m going in.

1416
02:09:50,840 --> 02:09:52,079
Dark Midwife!

1417
02:09:52,600 --> 02:09:54,159
Aktemur calm down.

1418
02:09:54,160 --> 02:09:55,599
Dark Midwife.

1419
02:09:57,520 --> 02:09:59,279
Dark Midwife.

1420
02:10:02,840 --> 02:10:05,639
Dark Midwife!
Say something, is everything okay?

1421
02:10:11,240 --> 02:10:13,439
Alcicek is okay.

1422
02:10:13,440 --> 02:10:15,039
How about the baby?

1423
02:10:15,040 --> 02:10:16,239
Is the baby okay?

1424
02:10:16,240 --> 02:10:18,679
Tell us? Is the baby okay?

1425
02:10:19,520 --> 02:10:20,919
Ayse Hatun.

1426
02:10:20,920 --> 02:10:23,719
...how long were yo pregnant with him?

1427
02:10:24,880 --> 02:10:26,919
If he's like this now...

1428
02:10:26,920 --> 02:10:28,679
...what will he do
when the baby comes?

1429
02:10:28,680 --> 02:10:30,599
Thank Allah.

1430
02:10:33,520 --> 02:10:35,039
Thank Allah.

1431
02:10:35,640 --> 02:10:36,799
Ulgen.

1432
02:10:36,800 --> 02:10:39,759
Go and tell the alps.
We'll sacrifice an animal.

1433
02:10:40,560 --> 02:10:41,879
Dark Midwife!

1434
02:10:41,880 --> 02:10:44,279
How are they? Say something.
What does this mean?

1435
02:10:44,280 --> 02:10:46,399
Come on son..

1436
02:10:46,400 --> 02:10:49,239
...both your hatun and baby are okay.

1437
02:10:49,240 --> 02:10:52,359
The wound wasn't very deep, you are lucky.

1438
02:10:52,360 --> 02:10:55,079
Go and see your hatun then.

1439
02:10:55,080 --> 02:10:56,319
Dark Midwife!

1440
02:10:56,320 --> 02:10:59,039
You gave me such good news,
ask anything you want from me.

1441
02:10:59,040 --> 02:11:01,799
-May Allah bless you!
-Go in now. Go.

1442
02:11:06,160 --> 02:11:08,199
Thank you so much.

1443
02:11:11,680 --> 02:11:13,119
So, Bengi...

1444
02:11:13,440 --> 02:11:16,599
We went through one more hardship
together, huh?

1445
02:11:16,600 --> 02:11:18,679
Thank Allah.

1446
02:11:24,000 --> 02:11:25,319
Thank Allah.

1447
02:11:47,840 --> 02:11:49,839
Brother.

1448
02:11:51,120 --> 02:11:52,799
Hold on. Hold on.

1449
02:11:56,280 --> 02:11:57,919
Those merciless..

1450
02:11:57,920 --> 02:12:00,159
Those lowlife dogs...

1451
02:12:00,160 --> 02:12:03,839
Hold on.

1452
02:12:16,560 --> 02:12:17,639
Are you okay?

1453
02:12:17,640 --> 02:12:18,519
Are you?

1454
02:12:18,520 --> 02:12:20,879
I'm okay my Bey.

1455
02:12:33,600 --> 02:12:35,119
Brother.

1456
02:12:35,120 --> 02:12:36,239
Are you okay brother?

1457
02:13:00,200 --> 02:13:02,159
What will we do now brother?

1458
02:13:02,160 --> 02:13:04,719
We will use those practices we had.

1459
02:13:16,200 --> 02:13:17,759
Brother they're coming.

1460
02:13:17,760 --> 02:13:18,919
Come on Alaeddin. Come on.

1461
02:13:46,640 --> 02:13:50,279
Sons..

1462
02:13:51,920 --> 02:13:53,159
Sons..

1463
02:14:22,440 --> 02:14:25,719
Brother... Sons..

1464
02:14:29,680 --> 02:14:32,879
Sons..

1465
02:14:37,840 --> 02:14:39,439
Brother stop.

1466
02:14:39,440 --> 02:14:41,439
Stop. It's a trap.

1467
02:14:46,360 --> 02:14:48,119
Be careful.

1468
02:14:54,840 --> 02:14:57,159
They put traps everywhere.

1469
02:14:58,880 --> 02:15:01,079
The hunt is about to become the prey.

1470
02:15:01,840 --> 02:15:03,439
Come on.

1471
02:15:13,000 --> 02:15:16,119
Just like how father taught.

1472
02:15:39,840 --> 02:15:42,399
Oh, Haqq!

1473
02:15:48,960 --> 02:15:50,839
Let's go

1474
02:15:54,720 --> 02:15:56,919
Over there!

1475
02:16:56,000 --> 02:16:57,079
My sons.

1476
02:17:04,280 --> 02:17:06,439
My sons.

1477
02:17:07,520 --> 02:17:10,159
We're going to find them, my Bey.

1478
02:17:15,520 --> 02:17:17,279
Let's get up.

1479
02:17:25,600 --> 02:17:26,879
Let's go.

1480
02:17:29,638 --> 02:17:31,759
We will not let them get away!

1481
02:17:32,480 --> 02:17:34,359
This will end!

1482
02:17:34,480 --> 02:17:38,108
I will stick Osman's head on the
edge of my sword!

1483
02:18:15,280 --> 02:18:18,439
Allah forbid,
what if they're in trouble, my Bey?

1484
02:18:18,799 --> 02:18:20,359
Sons.

1485
02:18:20,760 --> 02:18:22,119
My sons.

1486
02:18:22,920 --> 02:18:24,558
My sons...

1487
02:18:33,320 --> 02:18:34,919
Father!

1488
02:18:43,680 --> 02:18:45,397
Orhan.

1489
02:18:48,400 --> 02:18:50,279
Alaeddin.

1490
02:19:05,638 --> 02:19:09,119
Nayman!

1491
02:19:15,240 --> 02:19:18,316
Valens!

1492
02:19:26,240 --> 02:19:28,599
It's the end, Osman.

1493
02:19:29,480 --> 02:19:31,718
Your head will drop on the ground.

1494
02:19:32,480 --> 02:19:35,439
No.

1495
02:19:51,720 --> 02:19:57,239
You and your sons will die here,
Osman

1496
02:19:59,920 --> 02:20:04,599
Someone will pick up the flag after you, Osman.

1497
02:20:04,960 --> 02:20:07,959
But once all of you are dead...

1498
02:20:08,280 --> 02:20:12,839
...your names will be forgotten!

1499
02:20:21,920 --> 02:20:28,079
Let me tell you what's going to
happen after you die.

1500
02:20:31,240 --> 02:20:32,799
We will slaughter everyone!

1501
02:20:33,080 --> 02:20:37,879
...first in Yenisehir, then on all of your lands’!

1502
02:20:41,280 --> 02:20:45,039
I will retrieve everything you stole from Byzantium

1503
02:20:46,320 --> 02:20:51,679
The last thing you'll see on this world...

1504
02:20:52,600 --> 02:20:56,719
...will be the heads of your dead sons.

1505
02:21:05,680 --> 02:21:10,359
If you dare spill their blood...

1506
02:21:10,760 --> 02:21:15,559
..I will bury all of you here.

1507
02:21:19,560 --> 02:21:22,919
Now...

1508
02:21:26,160 --> 02:21:28,959
...let my sons go...

1509
02:21:29,840 --> 02:21:32,999
..and take me instead.

1510
02:22:08,156 --> 02:22:22,046
Visit our website for more: turkision.com